/* 心斋 · 剩余问答双语扩展（原中文题库不改） */
var ASK_BILINGUAL_MORE = {
'自卑、不自信、自我否定':{nameEn:'Low self-esteem and self-doubt',queryEn:'I feel like I am not good enough. I always doubt myself. I am afraid people will look down on me.',searchEn:'low self esteem insecure self doubt confidence worth failure',en:'Self-worth is not a verdict you have to earn. Replace a global label about yourself with one observable fact, keep a record of small things you did, and speak to yourself as you would to a friend in the same situation.',enZh:'自我价值不是需要争取才拿到的判决。把"我这个人不行"换成一件可观察的事实，记下自己做过的小事，并用你对待朋友的方式对自己说话。',terms:'self-esteem · self-criticism · core belief · self-compassion · evidence log',psychAnsEn:'Low self-esteem often turns one setback into a judgment about the whole person. Separate the event from your identity, record small completed actions, and compare yourself with your own past rather than everyone else.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not need to prove your worth before you deserve care. Take one small action with kindness toward yourself.',psychSupplementZh:'你不需要先证明自己的价值，才值得被照顾。带着对自己的善意，先完成一件小事。'},
'累、被掏空、职业倦怠':{queryEn:'I’m exhausted all the time. I don’t want to go to work. I feel burned out and empty.',nameEn:'Exhaustion and burnout',searchEn:'burnout exhaustion work stress fatigue empty overwhelmed rest',en:'Burnout is a signal of overload, not a personal weakness. Cut one commitment, replace scrolling with real rest, and check whether the workload itself needs to change.',enZh:'倦怠是超载的信号，不是个人脆弱。先砍掉一件承诺，把刷手机的"休息"换成真正的休息，再看是不是工作量本身需要调整。',terms:'burnout · exhaustion · emotional labor · recovery · workload',psychAnsEn:'Burnout is more than ordinary tiredness: it can include emotional exhaustion, cynicism, and a reduced sense of effectiveness. Restore boundaries, recovery, meaning, and support instead of relying on willpower alone.',psychSupplementEn:'Rest is not a reward for being productive. It is part of protecting the person who has been carrying too much.',psychSupplementZh:'休息不是做出成绩后才配得到的奖励，而是保护那个已经承担太多的自己。'},
'心乱、静不下来、杂念纷飞':{nameEn:'Restlessness and a busy mind',queryEn:'My mind will not settle down. I keep jumping from one thought to another. I cannot calm down or focus.',searchEn:'restless mind meditation thoughts calm focus mindfulness',en:'A restless mind settles through the body, not through force. Slow the out-breath, write the swirling thoughts in one line, and give the next ten minutes to a single task.',enZh:'纷乱的心要靠身体安下来，不靠硬压。把呼气放慢，用一句话写下翻腾的念头，再把接下来十分钟交给一件任务。',terms:'mental restlessness · grounding · slow breathing · attention · downshifting',psychAnsEn:'A busy mind is not a failure of meditation. Attention training means noticing that the mind has wandered and returning to one chosen anchor, such as the breath, without self-criticism.',psychSupplementEn:'Do not demand silence from the mind. One gentle return is already a moment of wisdom.',psychSupplementZh:'不要强迫心立刻安静。一次温柔地回来，本身就是一刻智慧。'},
'讨好型、不会拒绝、关系累':{queryEn:'I can’t say no to anyone. I always say yes and then feel exhausted. I’m scared of upsetting people.',nameEn:'People-pleasing and relationship exhaustion',searchEn:'people pleasing boundaries cannot say no relationships approval',en:'Saying yes to everything avoids conflict and costs you the relationship with yourself. Buy time before you answer, and decline one small request honestly this week.',enZh:'什么都答应，是躲开了冲突，代价是和自己的关系。先学会"我确认一下再回你"，这周诚实地拒绝一件小事。',terms:'people pleasing · assertiveness · boundary · fawn response · honest no',psychAnsEn:'People-pleasing often protects against the fear of rejection, but it hides your needs and builds resentment. Pause before agreeing, name your limit, and practice a clear respectful no.',psychSupplementEn:'A kind boundary is not a rejection of love. It lets care continue without abandoning yourself.',psychSupplementZh:'善意的边界不是拒绝爱，而是让关心能够持续，同时不抛下自己。'},
'患得患失、害怕失去':{nameEn:'Attachment anxiety and fear of loss',queryEn:'I am afraid of losing him. I keep checking on him. I never feel secure in this relationship.',searchEn:'attachment anxiety fear of abandonment relationship insecurity jealousy',en:'Fear of losing someone grows in the imagination more than in the facts. Check the evidence instead of reading silence, and put your energy into what you can do now.',enZh:'害怕失去，多半长在想象里而不在事实里。别把沉默当证据，先看事实，把力气放在此刻能做的那件事上。',terms:'attachment anxiety · reassurance seeking · uncertainty · security · present action',psychAnsEn:'Fear of loss can make you monitor and hold a relationship too tightly. Return attention to what you can offer and control, while building sources of safety that do not depend on another person alone.',psychSupplementEn:'Love can be held with an open hand. What is present deserves care, but it does not need to be possessed to be meaningful.',psychSupplementZh:'爱可以被一只放松的手托住。眼前的关系值得珍惜，但不必占有才有意义。'},
'空虚、人生没意义':{nameEn:'Emptiness and lack of meaning',queryEn:'I feel empty inside. Life feels meaningless to me. Nothing I do seems to matter.',searchEn:'emptiness meaning purpose existential depression life feels meaningless',en:'Meaning is usually built rather than found. Choose one thing you care about, do something concrete for another person, and let purpose grow out of repetition. If emptiness comes with thoughts of not wanting to live, tell a professional or someone you trust today.',enZh:'意义往往是做出来的，不是找出来的。选一件你在意的事，为别人做一件具体的实事，让意义从重复里长出来。如果空虚伴随"不想活了"的念头，请今天就告诉专业人士或可信任的人。',terms:'meaning in life · emptiness · values · contribution · safety',psychAnsEn:'Meaning is usually built through connection, contribution, learning, and chosen action rather than discovered as a perfect answer. Start with one activity that matters to you or helps another person.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not have to solve the meaning of life tonight. Make one small act of care, and let meaning grow from contact with life.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必今晚就解决人生意义。先做一个小小的关怀行动，让意义从与生活的接触中长出来。'},
'分手失恋、走不出情伤':{queryEn:'I can’t get over my ex. I still think about them all the time. I feel broken after the breakup.',nameEn:'Breakup grief and heartbreak',searchEn:'breakup heartbreak ex relationship grief move on loss',en:'Grief after a breakup is a real loss and needs time, not a deadline. Keep your daily routine, reduce contact and late-night checking, and let people who care about you be near.',enZh:'失恋是真实的丧失，需要时间而不需要期限。保住日常作息，减少联系和深夜翻看，让关心你的人留在身边。',terms:'breakup grief · loss · rumination · contact boundary · support',psychAnsEn:'Heartbreak is a real form of grief. Give the feelings a container, reduce repeated checking and rumination, rebuild daily routines, and allow recovery to take time rather than demanding instant closure.',psychSupplementEn:'You are not required to stop loving in order to begin living again. Let the relationship become part of your history, not the limit of your future.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必先停止爱过，才有资格重新生活。让这段关系成为经历，而不是未来的边界。'},
'社恐、不敢在人前说话':{queryEn:'I get nervous around people. I’m scared to speak in front of others. I avoid social situations.',nameEn:'Social anxiety and fear of speaking',searchEn:'social anxiety public speaking shy afraid people judgment exposure',en:'Social anxiety feeds on self-monitoring. Turn your attention outward, set one small exposure goal, stay a little longer than feels comfortable, and skip the post-event review.',enZh:'社交焦虑怕的是自我监视。把注意力转向外面，定一个小目标，比舒适多待一会儿，事后不做"复盘审判"。',terms:'social anxiety · exposure · self-focused attention · safety behavior · practice',psychAnsEn:'Social anxiety grows when avoidance teaches the brain that people are dangerous. Use gradual exposure, shift attention from self-monitoring to the conversation, and measure progress by participation rather than perfect confidence.',psychSupplementEn:'You may be nervous and still belong in the room. Courage is allowing yourself to be seen one small step at a time.',psychSupplementZh:'你可以紧张，也仍然有资格在场。勇气是一步一步允许自己被看见。'},
'和父母说不到一起、被催婚':{queryEn:'My parents keep pushing me to get married. We argue every time we talk. I can’t get along with them.',nameEn:'Conflict with parents and marriage pressure',searchEn:'parents conflict family pressure marriage pressure boundaries communication',en:'Some disagreements are differences, not problems to solve. State your position once without arguing, set a clear limit on the topic, and keep the parts of the relationship that are still warm.',enZh:'有些分歧是差异，不是要解决的问题。把立场平静说一次就够了，给话题划清界限，保留关系里还温暖的部分。',terms:'family conflict · boundaries · repeated argument · limit setting · differentiation',psychAnsEn:'Family conflict often mixes care, fear, expectations, and boundaries. Acknowledge their concern without handing over your decision, repeat your position calmly, and choose what information you want to share.',psychSupplementEn:'Respect does not require surrendering your life. You can love your parents and still walk at your own pace.',psychSupplementZh:'尊重不等于交出自己的人生。你可以爱父母，也可以按自己的节奏走。'},
'孩子不听话、青春期叛逆':{queryEn:'My kid doesn’t listen to me. My teenager talks back and plays on the phone all day.',nameEn:'Parenting conflict and adolescent resistance',searchEn:'parenting teenager rebellion child behavior screen time communication',en:'Adolescence is a push for independence, not a personal attack. Hold the few rules that matter, drop the constant correction, and keep one daily moment of connection with no agenda.',enZh:'青春期是在争取独立，不是针对你。守住少数真正重要的规则，减少不停纠正，每天留一个不带目的的连接时刻。',terms:'adolescence · autonomy · parenting · connection · consistent limits',psychAnsEn:'Adolescent resistance often signals a growing need for autonomy, not a bad character. Protect safety boundaries, offer limited choices, listen before correcting, and keep rules consistent rather than escalating punishment.',psychSupplementEn:'A child does not need a perfect parent. A steady adult who can repair after conflict is already a safe place.',psychSupplementZh:'孩子不需要完美父母。冲突后愿意修复、保持稳定的大人，本身就是安全的地方。'},
'总爱跟人比、心里不平衡':{nameEn:'Social comparison and envy',queryEn:'I keep comparing myself with others. They all seem to be doing better than me. I feel anxious and resentful.',searchEn:'social comparison envy jealousy insecurity others success',en:'Comparison is a habit of attention, and social media feeds it. Limit the scrolling, compare yourself with yourself last month, and name two things you actually value.',enZh:'比较是一种注意力习惯，社媒在喂养它。少刷一会儿，和自己上个月比，写下你真正看重的两件事。',terms:'social comparison · envy · social media · values · self-reference',psychAnsEn:'Comparison selectively shows another person’s highlights and your own shortcomings. Notice the comparison, return to your values, and turn useful admiration into a concrete learning step.',psychSupplementEn:'Another person’s light does not make yours smaller. You can acknowledge envy without letting it decide how you treat yourself.',psychSupplementZh:'别人的光不会让你的光变小。你可以承认嫉妒，但不必让它决定你如何对待自己。'},
'夫妻感情变淡、想分开':{queryEn:'My husband and I have nothing to say to each other. We feel distant. I even think about divorce.',nameEn:'Emotional distance in marriage',searchEn:'marriage relationship distant divorce communication intimacy conflict',en:'Distance usually grows through neglect rather than one big event. Rebuild small daily contact, name your own needs without blame, and try couples counseling before deciding to end it.',enZh:'感情变淡多是日积月累的忽略，不是某一件事。先恢复每天的小连接，用不带指责的方式说自己的需要；在决定分开前，试试专业的伴侣咨询。',terms:'emotional distance · couples counseling · repair · needs · decision',psychAnsEn:'Emotional distance often reflects a relationship account that has not been replenished. Create small regular moments of attention, make specific requests, and consider counseling when repeated repair attempts fail.',psychSupplementEn:'Do not decide the whole future in one exhausted night. First create one honest, safe conversation about what each person needs.',psychSupplementZh:'不要在一个疲惫的夜晚决定全部未来。先创造一次诚实而安全的谈话，说清彼此需要什么。'},
'伴侣出轨、要不要原谅':{nameEn:'Infidelity and rebuilding trust',queryEn:'My partner cheated on me. I do not know whether to forgive him or leave. I keep thinking about it and cannot trust him again.',searchEn:'infidelity betrayal cheating trust forgiveness divorce relationship',en:'Whether to continue after infidelity is a decision about trust, and it cannot be rushed. Insist on honesty and safety, decide nothing in the first shock, and get support while you think it through.',enZh:'出轨后要不要继续，是关于信任的决定，急不得。先要求诚实与安全，别在最初的震惊里做决定，想清楚的过程中先找到支持。',terms:'infidelity · trust repair · betrayal trauma · couple therapy · decision',psychAnsEn:'Betrayal creates a real injury to trust. Do not rush forgiveness or a final decision; first establish safety, truthful information, accountability, and whether both people are willing to repair the relationship.',psychSupplementEn:'Compassion for yourself may include distance, time, and a firm boundary. Forgiveness is not an obligation and does not erase consequences.',psychSupplementZh:'对自己的慈悲可以包括距离、时间和清楚的边界。原谅不是义务，也不会抹去后果。'},
'被人欺骗欺负、老实受气':{nameEn:'Being bullied, deceived, or taken advantage of',queryEn:'People take advantage of me and I cannot stand up for myself. I swallow my anger and feel it is unfair.',searchEn:'bullying being cheated exploited assertiveness boundaries conflict',en:'Being kind does not mean being available for harm. Say one clear stop sentence, keep records and witnesses, and tell someone who can act instead of absorbing it alone.',enZh:'善良不等于任人伤害。说一句清楚的"请停"，保留记录和见证，找能管这件事的人，而不是自己一个人吞下去。',terms:'bullying · boundary · assertiveness · documentation · support',psychAnsEn:'Being kind does not require accepting repeated harm. Document facts, seek support, set a short clear boundary, and use appropriate institutional or legal help when safety or money is involved.',psychSupplementEn:'Protecting yourself is not a betrayal of kindness. Compassion also means refusing to help harm continue.',psychSupplementZh:'保护自己不是背叛善良。慈悲也包括拒绝让伤害继续。'},
'失业、被裁、裸辞后迷茫':{queryEn:'I lost my job and can’t find a new one. I feel lost and scared to see people.',nameEn:'Job loss and career uncertainty',searchEn:'job loss unemployment layoff career uncertainty resume confidence',en:'Job loss shakes identity as well as income. Keep a daily structure, give the job search fixed hours instead of all day, and treat your worth as separate from your last title.',enZh:'失业动摇的不只是收入，还有身份感。保住日常结构，把求职放在固定时段而不是一整天，把"我是谁"和"上一份工作"分开。',terms:'job loss · identity · daily structure · job search · self-worth',psychAnsEn:'Job loss can shake both finances and identity. Separate your worth from a job title, restore a daily structure, treat applications as a process, and use small networking or learning steps to regain agency.',psychSupplementEn:'A lost role is not a lost self. Today’s small structure can become the bridge to the next chapter.',psychSupplementZh:'失去一个工作角色不等于失去自己。今天的小小秩序，可以成为通向下一章的桥。'},
'健康焦虑、老怀疑自己生病':{nameEn:'Health anxiety and fear of illness',queryEn:'I keep worrying that I am seriously ill. I check my symptoms online again and again. Even after the tests I still worry.',searchEn:'health anxiety illness anxiety hypochondria symptoms checking reassurance',en:'Health anxiety is fed by checking and searching. See a doctor once, agree on what to watch for, then stop the repeated body scanning and the late-night searching.',enZh:'健康焦虑靠反复检查和搜索喂养。找医生认真看一次，约定需要警惕的信号，然后停止不停的身体扫描和深夜搜索。',terms:'health anxiety · reassurance seeking · body checking · uncertainty · doctor visit',psychAnsEn:'Health anxiety is often maintained by a loop of bodily sensation, alarming interpretation, online checking, and brief reassurance. Follow appropriate medical advice, reduce repeated checking, and seek psychological support when worry takes over daily life.',psychSupplementEn:'Your fear is asking for safety, not punishment. Let qualified care check the body, while you gently stop feeding the endless search loop.',psychSupplementZh:'你的恐惧是在寻找安全感，不是在惩罚你。让专业医疗照看身体，同时温柔地停止无尽搜索。'},
'孤独、没朋友':{queryEn:'I feel lonely. I have no real friends to talk to. I’m always alone.',nameEn:'Loneliness and lack of connection',searchEn:'loneliness alone no friends isolation connection social support',en:'Loneliness eases through repeated small contact, not through one perfect friend. Reach out to one person this week, join something regular, and let the connection be ordinary.',enZh:'孤独靠重复的小接触缓解，不是等一个完美的朋友。这周主动联系一个人，加入一个固定活动，允许关系是普通的。',terms:'loneliness · social connection · belonging · repeated contact · community',psychAnsEn:'Loneliness is a signal of unmet connection, not proof that your personality is defective. Start with one low-pressure contact, a shared activity, or a weak social connection and build consistency over time.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not need a crowd to begin belonging. One honest hello can be the first thread back to the world.',psychSupplementZh:'你不需要先拥有一群人，才有资格归属。一句真诚的你好，就可能是回到世界的第一根线。'},
'脱单难、相亲内耗':{nameEn:'Dating fatigue and pressure to find a partner',queryEn:'I am single and cannot meet anyone. Dating feels like an exam and the blind dates exhaust me.',searchEn:'dating anxiety single matchmaking relationship pressure marriage',en:'Dating fatigue comes from treating every meeting as an exam. Decide what actually matters to you, keep a pace you can sustain, and let one meeting be just one meeting.',enZh:'相亲内耗，是因为把每次见面都当考试。先想清楚你真正在意的几条，把节奏放到能持续，让一次见面就只是一次见面。',terms:'dating fatigue · values · sustainable pace · rejection · expectation',psychAnsEn:'Dating is a process of fit, not a score for your worth. Replace the question “Will they choose me?” with “Do I feel safe and interested with them?” and keep your life meaningful outside dating.',psychSupplementEn:'Being single is not an unfinished identity. Meet people with curiosity, not as a trial where your worth is on judgment.',psychSupplementZh:'单身不是未完成的身份。带着好奇认识人，而不是把每次见面都当成审判价值的考试。'},
'刷手机停不下来、熬夜戒不掉':{queryEn:'I can’t stop scrolling on my phone. I stay up late every night and can’t stop.',nameEn:'Compulsive phone use and staying up late',searchEn:'phone addiction scrolling social media sleep late screen habit',en:'Late-night scrolling is a loop of stimulation and escape. Charge the phone away from the bed, set a shutdown time, and replace the last hour with one offline routine.',enZh:'深夜刷手机是"刺激—逃避"的循环。把手机放到床外充电，定一个关机时间，用一件线下的事替换睡前那一小时。',terms:'screen time · bedtime routine · stimulus control · self-regulation · sleep hygiene',psychAnsEn:'Endless scrolling is reinforced by variable rewards and easy access. Change the environment, charge the phone outside the bedroom, set a stopping ritual, and replace the habit with a low-stimulation activity.',psychSupplementEn:'Do not fight a highly designed system with shame alone. Make the kind choice easier by putting distance between you and the screen.',psychSupplementZh:'不要只用羞耻对抗精心设计的诱惑。把手机和自己拉开距离，让善待自己的选择更容易发生。'},
'缺钱、负债、经济压力焦虑':{queryEn:'I’m in debt and have no money. I panic every time a payment is due.',nameEn:'Debt and financial anxiety',searchEn:'debt money stress financial anxiety loans repayment poverty',en:'Money anxiety shrinks when the numbers become visible. Write down the real totals, pick one action you can take this month, and talk to a debt service instead of carrying it alone.',enZh:'把数字摊开，金钱焦虑才会缩小。写下真实的总额，挑一件这个月能做的行动，找债务咨询一起面对，别一个人扛。',terms:'financial stress · debt · budget · action plan · help seeking',psychAnsEn:'Financial anxiety grows in the dark. List every debt, interest rate, and minimum payment, stop taking new high-cost debt, and seek legitimate financial or legal advice to create a plan.',psychSupplementEn:'Debt is a circumstance, not a personality. Face one number at a time and protect food, sleep, and safety before shame.',psychSupplementZh:'债务是一种处境，不是人格。一次面对一个数字，并先保护吃饭、睡眠和安全，不让羞耻吞掉自己。'},
'产后崩溃、新手爸妈被掏空':{nameEn:'Postpartum overwhelm and parental exhaustion',queryEn:'Since the baby was born I cry all the time. I am exhausted and cannot sleep. I do not feel like myself anymore.',searchEn:'postpartum depression anxiety new parent baby sleep exhaustion crying',en:'Postpartum exhaustion is a medical and practical problem, not a failure of love. Protect sleep in shifts, accept concrete help, and get screened for postpartum depression.',enZh:'产后崩溃是医学和现实问题，不是"不够爱孩子"。用轮班守住睡眠，接受具体的帮忙，并按产后抑郁做一次筛查。',terms:'postpartum depression · sleep deprivation · shift care · support · screening',psychAnsEn:'Postpartum distress can be shaped by hormonal change, sleep deprivation, and isolation. Share the load, protect a block of sleep, speak with a healthcare professional when symptoms persist, and seek urgent help for safety concerns.',psychSupplementEn:'A baby needs a supported caregiver, not a flawless one. Asking someone to take a shift is an act of care for both of you.',psychSupplementZh:'孩子需要被支持的照顾者，而不是满分父母。请别人替你接一班，是同时照顾你们两个人。'},
'产后身材走样、恢复焦虑':{nameEn:'Postpartum body image and recovery anxiety',queryEn:'After giving birth my body has changed and I cannot accept it. I keep worrying about my weight and how I look.',searchEn:'postpartum body image weight recovery stretch marks self image',en:'A body that grew a child needs time, not punishment. Eat and sleep before training, return to movement gently when you are cleared, and ask whether the standard you are using is actually yours.',enZh:'生过孩子的身体需要时间，不需要惩罚。先把吃和睡顾好再谈运动，得到医生许可后温和恢复，并问自己：这个标准真的是你的吗？',terms:'body image · postpartum recovery · self-compassion · media standard · gentle exercise',psychAnsEn:'Postpartum bodies need time and medical recovery, not comparison with edited images. Shift from returning to an old body toward caring for the body that carried you, and seek assessment before intense exercise.',psychSupplementEn:'Your body is not a failed project. It carried you through something immense and deserves patience rather than punishment.',psychSupplementZh:'你的身体不是一个失败的项目。它带你经历了巨大的事情，值得耐心，而不是惩罚。'},
'带娃方式跟婆婆/老人分歧':{nameEn:'Parenting disagreements with grandparents',queryEn:'My mother in law and I argue about how to raise the child. We have very different ideas about parenting. I feel judged in my own home.',searchEn:'parenting grandparents in laws childcare family conflict boundaries',en:'Childcare disagreements are often about authority, not the details. Agree the few non-negotiable rules with your partner first, then speak with one voice on safety matters.',enZh:'育儿分歧常常是"谁说了算"，不是细节。先和伴侣谈定少数底线，涉及安全的事由你们两个人用同一个声音说。',terms:'co-parenting · intergenerational conflict · unified front · safety rules · negotiation',psychAnsEn:'Separate safety issues from preferences and style differences. Set clear non-negotiable boundaries, invite help within defined limits, and use a pediatric professional when facts are disputed.',psychSupplementEn:'Different generations may use different maps while wanting the same child to be safe. Protect the boundary without turning the helper into an enemy.',psychSupplementZh:'不同代人可能拿着不同地图，却都希望孩子平安。守住边界，也不要把来帮忙的人变成敌人。'},
'产假结束怕回职场、全职后想复出':{nameEn:'Returning to work after childcare',queryEn:'My maternity leave is over and I am afraid to go back to work. I have been at home for years and worry I cannot catch up.',searchEn:'return to work after maternity leave stay at home parent career gap',en:'Going back to work is a transition, not a test of motherhood. Plan childcare and the first two weeks in detail, expect a dip in energy, and re-enter gradually if you can.',enZh:'回职场是一次过渡，不是"当妈的考试"。把托育和头两周安排写细，允许精力暂时下滑，能循序渐进就别一步到位。',terms:'return to work · transition · childcare plan · identity shift · gradual re-entry',psychAnsEn:'Returning to work is an adjustment, not a test of your worth. Plan childcare trials, clarify expectations, describe caregiving skills as real skills, and use gradual steps if a full return feels too large.',psychSupplementEn:'Caring for a child did not erase your abilities. You are allowed to rebuild your work life at a humane pace.',psychSupplementZh:'照顾孩子没有抹去你的能力。你可以用对人友善的速度重新建立工作生活。'},
'年龄焦虑、一事无成、怕来不及':{nameEn:'Age anxiety and fear of being behind',queryEn:'I am afraid I am running out of time. I have not achieved anything yet. My friends are all ahead of me.',searchEn:'age anxiety behind peers 30 35 life progress success',en:'Age panic comes from comparing your timeline with an imaginary one. Define what finishing actually means to you, take the first step this month, and drop the milestones that are not yours.',enZh:'年龄焦虑，是拿你的时间和一个想象中的时间表比。写清"完成"对你到底指什么，这个月就走第一步，删掉不属于你的里程碑。',terms:'age anxiety · social clock · life timeline · values · first step',psychAnsEn:'Age anxiety is often amplified by social clocks and selective comparison. Replace inherited deadlines with values you actually chose, then invest in small repeatable actions that compound over time.',psychSupplementEn:'Your life is not late because it does not match someone else’s calendar. A sincere next step still counts at every age.',psychSupplementZh:'你的人生没有因为不同于别人的日历就迟到。无论什么年龄，真诚的下一步都算数。'},
'怕变老、初老焦虑':{nameEn:'Fear of aging',queryEn:'I am afraid of getting old. I see wrinkles and grey hair and it scares me. I do not want to age.',searchEn:'fear of aging getting old wrinkles age anxiety body changes',en:'Growing older is a physical fact and also a story you tell about it. Keep strength, sleep and contact with people you like, and notice how much of the fear is about being seen differently.',enZh:'变老既是身体事实，也是你讲给自己的一套故事。守住力量、睡眠和喜欢的社交，并看看这份恐惧里有多少是怕"被看得不一样了"。',terms:'aging anxiety · life stage · health habits · self-image · meaning',psychAnsEn:'Aging is not the same as losing all strength or value. Focus on health behaviors, relationships, learning, and realistic medical care instead of fighting every visible change.',psychSupplementEn:'The body changes, but your capacity for care and wisdom can deepen. Thank the body for carrying you this far.',psychSupplementZh:'身体会变化，但关怀与智慧可以更深。谢谢这副身体带你走到今天。'},
'后悔当初、总想"如果当时"':{nameEn:'Regret and “what if” thinking',queryEn:'I keep thinking about the past. I wish I had chosen differently. I cannot let it go.',searchEn:'regret what if past choices guilt counterfactual thinking',en:'Hindsight always looks clearer than the moment felt. Write down what you actually knew at the time, take one lesson from it, and put the energy into a decision you can make now.',enZh:'事后看总是比当时清楚。写下你当时真正知道的信息，取出一条经验，把力气转到此刻还能做的决定上。',terms:'regret · counterfactual thinking · hindsight bias · acceptance · next decision',psychAnsEn:'Regret often judges an earlier self with information gained later. Acknowledge what the choice taught you, repair what can be repaired, and use the lesson to guide the next decision rather than punish the past.',psychSupplementEn:'The past version of you acted with the information available then. Offer that person understanding, and let today make the next honest choice.',psychSupplementZh:'过去的你只能依据当时拥有的信息行动。请理解那个自己，让今天的你做出下一次诚实选择。'},
'工作没有价值感、上班没意义':{nameEn:'Meaningless work and loss of purpose',queryEn:'My work feels meaningless. I see no point in it. I drag myself to the office every day.',searchEn:'meaningless work career purpose job dissatisfaction burnout',en:'Meaning at work rarely arrives on its own. Name what you actually want to contribute, look for one task that fits it, and plan a longer move instead of quitting in a bad week.',enZh:'工作的意义很少自己送上门。写清你真正想贡献什么，先找一件对得上的任务，再规划更长的转向，而不是在难受的一周里裸辞。',terms:'work meaning · engagement · job crafting · career plan · burnout',psychAnsEn:'Work meaning can come from contribution, mastery, autonomy, and connection, not only from a perfect job title. Identify which need is missing and test a small change before making a major career decision.',psychSupplementEn:'Your job may be one part of life, not the judge of your life. Bring care to one useful task and keep building meaning beyond the office.',psychSupplementZh:'工作可以是生活的一部分，不是审判生活的法官。认真完成一件有用的小事，也在工作之外继续建立意义。'},
'作息紊乱、黑白颠倒、想改改不过来':{nameEn:'Disrupted sleep schedule and reversed day-night rhythm',queryEn:'My days and nights are reversed. I sleep in the daytime and stay awake all night. I want to change but I cannot.',searchEn:'sleep schedule circadian rhythm night owl wake up routine jet lag',en:'The body clock shifts through mornings, not through willpower. Fix one waking time for a week, get light early, and move bedtime only after the wake time holds.',enZh:'生物钟靠早晨拨回来，不靠意志力。先把起床时间固定一周，早上见光，等起床稳住之后再提前睡觉。',terms:'circadian rhythm · wake time · morning light · consistency · sleep drive',psychAnsEn:'A stable wake time is usually a stronger anchor than forcing an early bedtime. Use morning light, regular meals, limited naps, and gradual evening dimming to reset the rhythm.',psychSupplementEn:'Do not demand a perfect schedule in one night. A steady morning repeated patiently can teach the body its way home.',psychSupplementZh:'不要要求身体一夜之间完美改好。耐心重复一个稳定的早晨，身体会慢慢找到回家的路。'},
'拖延、拖到最后一刻、计划总破功':{nameEn:'Procrastination and broken plans',queryEn:'I keep putting things off until the last minute. My plans always fall apart. I just cannot make myself start.',searchEn:'procrastination deadline self discipline planning habits avoidance',en:'Procrastination is usually avoidance of a feeling, not laziness. Shrink the task to a two-minute start, begin in the same place each time, and forgive one lapse instead of quitting.',enZh:'拖延多半是在躲一种感受，不是懒。把任务缩到"两分钟就能开始"，固定在同一个地方起步，允许一次失手，而不是就此放弃。',terms:'procrastination · task initiation · avoidance · implementation intention · self-forgiveness',psychAnsEn:'Procrastination often avoids the discomfort of starting rather than the task itself. Shrink the first step, use an implementation intention, create an external deadline, and replace self-attack with a restart.',psychSupplementEn:'A delayed start is not a permanent identity. Begin again with two minutes; returning is more useful than punishment.',psychSupplementZh:'晚开始不等于固定的身份。先用两分钟重新开始，回来比惩罚自己更有用。'},
'害怕做决定、选择困难':{nameEn:'Decision anxiety and difficulty choosing',queryEn:'I am afraid of making the wrong choice. I keep going back and forth. I often regret what I decided.',searchEn:'decision anxiety choice overload indecisive fear wrong choice regret',en:'More options do not make choosing easier. Set a deadline for the decision, list the two criteria that really matter, and accept a good-enough option instead of the perfect one.',enZh:'选项越多，越难决定。给决定设一个期限，只列真正重要的两条标准，接受"够好"，而不是非要"最好"。',terms:'decision paralysis · choice overload · good enough · deadline · criteria',psychAnsEn:'Decision paralysis grows when every choice is treated as irreversible and perfect. Separate reversible from major decisions, set a deadline, choose “good enough,” and invest in making the chosen path work.',psychSupplementEn:'There may be no choice without uncertainty. Wisdom is choosing with care, then meeting the path in front of you.',psychSupplementZh:'也许没有一个完全没有不确定性的选择。智慧是认真选择，然后走好眼前的路。'},
'亲人离世、走不出来':{queryEn:'I lost someone close to me and can’t move on. I cry whenever I think of them.',nameEn:'Grief after losing someone',searchEn:'grief bereavement death loss mourning cannot move on',en:'Grief does not follow a schedule. Let the waves come, keep small routines, and say their name out loud; seek grief counseling if you feel stuck or daily life stops working.',enZh:'哀伤不按日程表走。允许情绪一波波来，保住小的作息，把他们的名字说出来；如果长期卡住或生活转不动，请寻求哀伤辅导。',terms:'grief · bereavement · mourning · continuing bonds · grief counseling',psychAnsEn:'Grief has no fixed timetable and does not require forgetting. Keep a continuing bond through memory or meaningful ritual, protect basic routines, and seek professional help when grief remains overwhelming.',psychSupplementEn:'Love does not have to disappear for life to continue. Let the bond change shape and carry one warm thing forward.',psychSupplementZh:'爱不必消失，生活才可以继续。让这份连接换一种形状，带着一件温暖的东西向前走。'},
'家人重病临终、要不要救、怎么告别':{nameEn:'End-of-life care and saying goodbye',queryEn:'My family member is dying and I have to decide about treatment. I do not know how to say goodbye. I feel I have to choose for them.',searchEn:'end of life palliative care hospice family illness medical decisions goodbye caregiver',en:'End-of-life choices are made with the doctors and the patient, not alone in a corridor. Ask about prognosis and comfort care, record what the patient wanted, and say the words you want to say now.',enZh:'临终抉择要和医生、和病人一起做，不该一个人在走廊里决定。问清预后与舒缓方案，记下病人自己的意愿，想说的话现在就说。',terms:'end of life · advance care planning · palliative care · farewell · family decision',psychAnsEn:'When cure is no longer possible, palliative care focuses on comfort, dignity, and the patient’s wishes. Ask clinicians about benefits and burdens, involve the patient when possible, share caregiving, and say what needs to be said.',psychSupplementEn:'Being present does not mean controlling the outcome. Gentle companionship, honest words, and relief from suffering are meaningful forms of love.',psychSupplementZh:'陪伴不等于控制结果。温柔在场、诚实说话、减少痛苦，都是有意义的爱。'},
'怕死、一想到死就心慌':{queryEn:'I’m scared of dying. At night I panic when I think about death.',nameEn:'Death anxiety',searchEn:'death anxiety fear of dying existential anxiety panic meaning',en:'Death anxiety usually grows in silence and shrinks in daylight. Say the fear out loud to someone, return to ordinary life today, and explore what matters to you while you still have time.',enZh:'死亡恐惧常在沉默里长大。把这份害怕说给一个人听，今天先回到日常生活，并趁还有时间去想：什么对你真正重要。',terms:'death anxiety · mortality · existential · values · talking it through',psychAnsEn:'Death anxiety is a human response to finitude. Notice the fear without debating it at night, return to the present, and translate “I am afraid to die” into one life-giving action or conversation.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not have to defeat mortality to live meaningfully. Let the awareness of impermanence return you to the people and moments here now.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必战胜无常，才有资格有意义地生活。觉知无常，可以把你带回此刻的人与事。'},
'确诊重病、怕时日不多':{nameEn:'Facing a serious diagnosis',queryEn:'I was diagnosed with a serious illness. I am afraid I do not have much time left. I do not know how to tell my family.',searchEn:'serious illness cancer diagnosis limited time fear dying meaning',en:'A serious diagnosis brings fear and practical questions at the same time. Ask about treatment aims and symptom control, bring one person to appointments, and take life in shorter horizons.',enZh:'确诊重病，恐惧和现实问题会一起压来。问清治疗目标与症状控制，看病时带上一个人，把日子切成更短的段落来过。',terms:'serious illness · prognosis · symptom control · supportive care · pacing',psychAnsEn:'A serious diagnosis can bring shock, fear, and a search for meaning. Seek clear medical information, emotional support, symptom care, advance planning, and one present-focused day at a time.',psychSupplementEn:'You are more than a diagnosis and more than a countdown. Let today contain care, truth, and one moment of connection.',psychSupplementZh:'你不等于诊断，也不等于倒计时。让今天拥有照顾、真实和一刻连接。'},
'怕父母变老、怕他们离开':{nameEn:'Fear of losing aging parents',queryEn:'I am afraid of my parents getting old and leaving me. I get scared when I think about that day. I want to spend more time with them.',searchEn:'parents aging anticipatory grief fear loss family care',en:'This fear is love with nowhere to go. Turn it into time: ask about their health and wishes, record their stories, and let today be ordinary company instead of rehearsal for goodbye.',enZh:'这份怕，是爱没有出口。把它变成时间：问问他们的健康和心愿，记下他们的故事，把今天过成普通的陪伴，而不是告别的预演。',terms:'anticipatory grief · aging parents · presence · life review · planning',psychAnsEn:'Anticipatory grief can turn love into constant fear. Convert worry into present connection and practical preparation, while allowing uncertainty to remain uncertainty.',psychSupplementEn:'The future cannot be secured by rehearsing its pain. Let fear become a phone call, a meal, or a shared walk today.',psychSupplementZh:'反复预演未来的痛，无法让未来更安全。让恐惧变成今天的一通电话、一顿饭或一次同行。'},
'养老焦虑、怕老无所依':{nameEn:'Retirement and elder-care anxiety',queryEn:'I worry about who will take care of me when I am old. I am afraid of being alone and helpless in my old age.',searchEn:'retirement anxiety pension aging care loneliness financial planning',en:'Aging well is arranged in concrete pieces, not settled by worry. Clarify money, housing and care preferences, build relationships outside the family, and start with one item this month.',enZh:'养老要靠一件件具体的事安排，不靠焦虑。把经济、居住和照护意愿写清，在家以外也建立关系，这个月先动一项。',terms:'retirement planning · long-term care · housing · social network · preparation',psychAnsEn:'Retirement anxiety becomes more manageable when translated into plans for finances, health, housing, and relationships. Build more than one source of support instead of relying on a single person.',psychSupplementEn:'Preparing for later life is care, not panic. Build practical support while also allowing yourself to live this current season.',psychSupplementZh:'为晚年准备是照顾，不是恐慌。建立现实支持，也允许自己好好生活当前这一季。'},
'房价下跌、买房被套、亏了怎么办':{nameEn:'Housing loss and mortgage anxiety',queryEn:'The house price dropped and I am stuck with the mortgage. I do not know whether to sell it and take the loss. It keeps me up at night.',searchEn:'house price fall mortgage loss property anxiety sunk cost sell home',en:'A market loss is a fact, while panic selling is a decision you can still avoid. Check the real numbers, ask whether the choice still suits your life, and get neutral advice before acting.',enZh:'账面亏损是事实，恐慌卖出却仍是可以避免的决定。先算清真实数字，问自己这套选择还适合现在的生活吗，行动前找立场中立的人商量。',terms:'financial loss · sunk cost · market volatility · decision under stress · neutral advice',psychAnsEn:'Do not let the original purchase price make every future decision. Compare present options, affordability, use, and risk; separate sunk cost from the choice that protects life now.',psychSupplementEn:'A home is meant to support living, not consume the whole mind. Protect sleep and basic stability before protecting a number on paper.',psychSupplementZh:'房子本该支持生活，不该吞掉整颗心。先保护睡眠和基本稳定，再保护账面上的数字。'},
'贷款逾期、断供、被催收快撑不住了':{nameEn:'Loan default and collection pressure',queryEn:'I missed my loan payments and the collectors keep calling me. I cannot keep up with it anymore. I do not know where to turn.',searchEn:'loan default debt collection foreclosure financial crisis cannot cope',en:'Debt pressure needs contact, not silence. Talk to the lender about a restructuring plan, get free debt counseling, and never take a new high-interest loan to cover the old one.',enZh:'债务压力要靠沟通解决，不是躲。主动找机构谈展期或重组，寻求免费的债务咨询，绝不要用新的高息借款去填旧洞。',terms:'overdue debt · restructuring · debt counseling · collection pressure · crisis plan',psychAnsEn:'Debt panic improves when avoidance stops. List the facts, stop taking new high-cost debt, contact legitimate lenders early, protect basic needs, and seek legal or financial advice when necessary.',psychSupplementEn:'A debt is urgent, but it is not your identity and it is never worth losing your life. Bring another person into the plan today.',psychSupplementZh:'债务很急，但不是你的身份，更不值得用生命偿还。今天就让另一个可信任的人参与计划。'},
'要不要生孩子、不敢生':{nameEn:'Uncertainty about having children',queryEn:'I do not know whether to have a child. I am afraid of the responsibility and the cost. Everyone keeps asking me.',searchEn:'whether to have children reproductive choice fear parenting pressure',en:'This decision belongs to you and your partner, not to the pressure around you. Separate what you want from what you fear, list the real conditions, and accept that no option is risk free.',enZh:'这个决定属于你和伴侣，不属于周围的催促。把"我想要"和"我害怕"分开，列清现实条件，并接受没有一个选项是没有风险的。',terms:'reproductive decision · ambivalence · autonomy · values · couple communication',psychAnsEn:'Having children is a major personal decision, not a deadline set by family or society. Explore both possible futures, practical support, values, and consent between partners without forcing certainty overnight.',psychSupplementEn:'There is no single life script that makes a person complete. Let the decision come from a steady heart, not from fear or pressure.',psychSupplementZh:'没有一条人生剧本能让人因此完整。让决定来自安稳的心，而不是恐惧或催促。'},
'考试压力大、怕考不上、升学焦虑':{nameEn:'Exam pressure and academic anxiety',queryEn:'I am afraid I will fail the exam. I panic before every test and cannot sleep. The pressure to get in is too much.',searchEn:'exam anxiety test pressure school study failure university entrance',en:'Exam anxiety responds to structure more than to reassurance. Study in fixed blocks with real breaks, rehearse under time pressure, and separate your worth from one score.',enZh:'考试焦虑靠结构缓解，不靠安慰。用固定时段加上真正的休息来复习，按时间压力做模拟，并把"我值多少"和一个分数分开。',terms:'test anxiety · study plan · timed rehearsal · self-worth · performance',psychAnsEn:'Exam anxiety grows when one test is treated as a verdict on an entire life. Prepare with realistic practice, protect sleep, focus on the next question, and separate performance from personal worth.',psychSupplementEn:'An exam can measure a performance, not the whole person. Do the next honest piece of work and let the result be only one part of your story.',psychSupplementZh:'考试可以测一次表现，不能测完整的人。认真完成下一小步，让结果只成为你故事的一部分。'},
'反复想一件事、反复检查、洁癖强迫':{nameEn:'Obsessive thoughts and repeated checking',queryEn:'I keep thinking about the same thing and checking it again and again. I wash my hands many times a day. I cannot stop even when I want to.',searchEn:'OCD intrusive thoughts compulsive checking contamination washing ERP',en:'Checking brings relief for minutes and strengthens the loop. Delay the ritual instead of fighting it, limit it to agreed times, and consider CBT with exposure and response prevention.',enZh:'反复检查换来的只是几分钟的安心，却让循环更牢。用"延迟"代替硬扛，把仪式限制在约定的时段；可以考虑暴露与反应阻止的认知行为治疗。',terms:'obsessive compulsive · checking · ERP · ritual delay · CBT',psychAnsEn:'Intrusive thoughts are not intentions and compulsions offer only short relief. Evidence-based treatment such as exposure and response prevention helps people allow uncertainty without repeating the ritual; seek professional assessment when it interferes with life.',psychSupplementEn:'A frightening thought is not a command and does not define your character. You deserve support, not endless reassurance or self-blame.',psychSupplementZh:'可怕的念头不是命令，也不定义你的品格。你值得得到帮助，而不是无尽确认或自责。'},
'突然心跳很快、喘不上气、感觉要死了':{nameEn:'Panic attacks and fear of dying',queryEn:'Suddenly my heart races and I cannot breathe. I feel like I am going to die. It comes out of nowhere.',searchEn:'panic attack heart racing shortness breath dizziness dying fear',en:'A panic surge is frightening but not dangerous. Rule out physical causes once, slow your out-breath, stay where you are instead of running, and let the wave pass.',enZh:'惊恐发作很吓人，但本身不危险。先排查一次躯体原因，把呼气放慢，留在原地不逃，让这波过去。',terms:'panic attack · hyperventilation · medical check · breathing · exposure',psychAnsEn:'After medical causes have been assessed, panic can be understood as a false alarm that feels intensely real. Use slow exhalation, label the wave, and work with a professional on gradual exposure rather than avoiding every bodily sensation.',psychSupplementEn:'A wave can be frightening without being a prophecy. Stay with the next breath and seek urgent care if symptoms are new, severe, or medically uncertain.',psychSupplementZh:'一阵强烈的感觉可以很吓人，却不一定是预言。先陪伴下一口呼吸；若症状新发、严重或无法确定，请及时就医。'},
'压力一大就胃疼头疼、身上各种不舒服':{nameEn:'Stress-related physical symptoms',queryEn:'When I am stressed my stomach hurts and I get headaches. I feel tight in the chest. The doctors say nothing is wrong.',searchEn:'somatic symptoms stress stomach headache chest tightness psychosomatic',en:'Stress often appears in the body before it can be put into words. Get one proper check-up for safety, then work on the body and the pressure together: sleep, meals, movement, one fewer demand.',enZh:'压力常常先落在身体上，才被说出来。为稳妥做一次检查，然后身体和压力一起调：睡眠、三餐、活动量，再减掉一件要求。',terms:'somatization · stress response · medical check · lifestyle · load reduction',psychAnsEn:'Unexplained symptoms can be real and stress-sensitive without being imaginary. Complete appropriate medical evaluation, track triggers, reduce repeated reassurance seeking, and give emotions a safe outlet.',psychSupplementEn:'Your body is not betraying you; it may be communicating overload. Listen with care while continuing appropriate medical follow-up.',psychSupplementZh:'身体没有背叛你，它可能正在表达过载。带着关心去倾听，同时继续合适的医疗随访。'},
'一有压力就暴食、情绪性进食管不住嘴':{queryEn:'I eat too much when I’m stressed. I can’t control my eating and feel guilty after.',nameEn:'Emotional eating and binge urges',searchEn:'emotional eating binge eating stress food cravings diet guilt',en:'Emotional eating is usually an attempt to soothe, not a lack of discipline. Eat regularly so hunger is never extreme, name the feeling before the fridge, and get help if binges feel out of control.',enZh:'情绪性进食多半是在自我安抚，不是没自制力。先把三餐吃稳、别让自己饿到极点，开冰箱前先给情绪命名；如果失控感明显，请寻求专业帮助。',terms:'emotional eating · binge eating · soothing · regular meals · professional help',psychAnsEn:'Emotional eating often regulates distress for a short time and then adds guilt. Regular meals, a pause to identify the feeling, alternative soothing actions, and professional help for recurrent binges are more effective than harsh restriction.',psychSupplementEn:'One episode does not make you bad or ruin your body. Replace punishment with the next caring meal and seek support when control feels impossible.',psychSupplementZh:'一次失控不会让你变坏，也不会毁掉身体。用下一顿温和的饭代替惩罚；若无法控制，请寻求帮助。'},
'原生家庭的伤总在重演、总重复父母的相处模式':{queryEn:'I keep repeating my parents’ patterns. My childhood still hurts me today.',nameEn:'Repeating family patterns and childhood wounds',searchEn:'childhood trauma family patterns attachment inner child repetition',en:'Patterns repeat because they were learned early and feel familiar. Notice the moment the old script starts, try one different response, and consider therapy to work on it in depth.',enZh:'模式会重演，因为它是早年学会的、很熟悉的。留意旧剧本启动的那一刻，试着换一个反应，并考虑用咨询深入处理。',terms:'family of origin · intergenerational pattern · awareness · different response · therapy',psychAnsEn:'Familiar relationship patterns can feel safe even when they hurt. Notice the trigger, name the old script, practice a new response, and consider therapy when the pattern repeatedly harms close relationships.',psychSupplementEn:'The past may explain a pattern without owning your future. You can honor the child who survived and teach the adult a different way.',psychSupplementZh:'过去可以解释一种模式，却不能拥有你的未来。你可以安慰曾经努力活下来的孩子，也教现在的自己走另一条路。'},
'回避型依恋、喜欢一个人又想逃':{nameEn:'Avoidant attachment and fear of intimacy',queryEn:'When someone gets too close I want to run away. I like him but I push him away. I am afraid of being close to anyone.',searchEn:'avoidant attachment intimacy fear closeness push away relationships',en:'The urge to pull away is self-protection, and it can be worked with. Stay for one more honest conversation instead of disappearing, and say what you need instead of leaving it unsaid.',enZh:'想逃是一种自我保护，但它可以被练习。多留一次对话、别直接消失，把"我需要什么"说出来，而不是留白。',terms:'avoidant attachment · intimacy · deactivation · honest conversation · therapy',psychAnsEn:'Avoidance often protects against feared dependence or rejection, but it can also block safe closeness. Communicate your need for space, practice small doses of honesty, and seek attachment-focused support when the pattern repeats.',psychSupplementEn:'Needing space does not make you incapable of love. Say “I need a pause, not an ending,” and let trust grow in small steps.',psychSupplementZh:'需要空间不等于没有爱的能力。试着说“我需要暂停，不是结束”，让信任一点一点生长。'},
'高敏感、心思重、总在意别人的脸色和话':{queryEn:'I overthink what people say to me. I’m too sensitive and worry they don’t like me.',nameEn:'High sensitivity and over-reading others',searchEn:'high sensitivity HSP overthinking people pleasing reading faces social anxiety',en:'High sensitivity means taking in more input, not having a flaw. Protect your daily capacity, check your interpretations against facts, and give yourself real recovery time after intense contact.',enZh:'高敏感是接收到的信息更多，不是缺陷。守住每天的承载力，把猜测拿去和事实核对，密集接触之后给自己真正的恢复时间。',terms:'high sensitivity · sensory load · interpretation · recovery · capacity',psychAnsEn:'Sensitivity can be a strength, but mind-reading and rumination turn it into exhaustion. Check the evidence, ask directly when appropriate, schedule a stopping point, and protect sleep and recovery.',psychSupplementEn:'Your sensitivity is not a sentence. Let it become empathy with boundaries, not a reason to monitor every face in the room.',psychSupplementZh:'敏感不是判决。让它成为有边界的共情，而不是监控房间里每一张脸的理由。'},
'完美主义、对自己太苛刻':{nameEn:'Perfectionism and harsh self-criticism',queryEn:'I have to do everything perfectly. I am too hard on myself. One small mistake and I blame myself for days.',searchEn:'perfectionism self criticism high standards mistakes fear failure',en:'Perfectionism raises the standard and lowers the satisfaction. Define done in advance, allow a good-enough version, and speak to yourself in the tone you would use with a colleague.',enZh:'完美主义把标准抬高，把满足感压低。事先定义"做完"的样子，允许够好的版本，用你对同事的口气对自己说话。',terms:'perfectionism · self-criticism · good enough · standards · self-compassion',psychAnsEn:'Perfectionism ties worth to flawless outcomes and can create procrastination. Try a “good enough” experiment, review errors without insulting yourself, and separate excellence from the demand to be perfect.',psychSupplementEn:'You are allowed to be a person while learning. A humane standard can make better work possible.',psychSupplementZh:'你可以一边学习，一边只是一个普通人。更人道的标准，反而可能让事情做得更好。'},
'恐婚、一想到结婚就害怕想逃':{nameEn:'Fear of marriage and commitment',queryEn:'I am afraid of getting married. Just thinking about the wedding makes me want to run away. I am scared of being tied down.',searchEn:'fear of marriage commitment wedding anxiety relationship escape',en:'Fear of marriage usually carries a concern worth reading. Name what specifically frightens you, discuss it plainly with your partner, and slow the timeline instead of forcing it.',enZh:'恐婚里往往藏着一个值得读的担心。把具体怕什么写出来，和伴侣坦白谈，把节奏放慢，而不是硬推自己。',terms:'fear of marriage · commitment · premarital counseling · specific fears · pacing',psychAnsEn:'Marriage anxiety may reflect uncertainty, fear of losing autonomy, or unanswered practical questions. Discuss money, boundaries, children, care, and conflict before deciding; clarity is kinder than avoidance.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not need to promise forever while hiding fear. Bring the fear into a safe conversation and let truth guide the next step.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必在藏着恐惧时承诺永远。把恐惧带进安全的谈话，让真实引导下一步。'},
'孕期焦虑、怀孕后总担心想哭':{nameEn:'Pregnancy anxiety and emotional distress',queryEn:'I am pregnant and worried all the time. I am afraid something is wrong with the baby and I cry easily.',searchEn:'pregnancy anxiety prenatal depression worry crying baby health birth',en:'Pregnancy anxiety deserves care, not dismissal. Bring your fears to prenatal professionals, limit alarming searches, build practical support, and seek perinatal mental-health care when distress persists.',enZh:'孕期焦虑需要被照顾，而不是被轻描淡写。把担心告诉产检专业人员，减少令人恐慌的搜索，建立支持；如果痛苦持续，请寻求围产期心理帮助。',psychMainEn:'First, know that strong emotions during pregnancy are not fussiness or overthinking. Hormonal shifts, a major identity change, and physical discomfort can arrive together, and the emotional system is affected as well. If anxiety, insomnia, catastrophic thoughts, or loss of appetite persist, prenatal anxiety or depression deserves proper care. Write down fears and ask the doctor about them at the next check-up instead of treating late-night searches as medical advice. Replace the demand to be a perfect mother with practical support: keep an emotional outlet, and tell your family that you need company and listening, not judgment.',terms:'prenatal anxiety · perinatal depression · worry · support · screening',psychAnsEn:'Pregnancy can bring hormonal, physical, and identity changes that intensify anxiety. Bring fears to prenatal professionals, limit alarming searches, build practical support, and seek perinatal mental-health care when distress persists.',psychSupplementEn:'Worry does not make you a bad parent. A supported and cared-for mother is already giving the baby something important.',psychSupplementZh:'担心不会让你成为坏妈妈。一个被支持、被照顾的妈妈，已经在给孩子重要的东西。'},
'备孕很久怀不上、久备不孕压力大':{nameEn:'Infertility stress and prolonged trying to conceive',queryEn:'We have been trying to conceive for a long time and nothing happens. Every month I am disappointed. The pressure is too much.',searchEn:'trying to conceive infertility stress fertility treatment pregnancy pressure',en:'Infertility is a medical issue and a grief at the same time. Get a proper evaluation early, limit how much time you give to talking about it, and keep the couple relationship bigger than the goal.',enZh:'不孕既是医学问题，也是丧失。尽早做正规评估，给"谈这件事"设个时间上限，让夫妻关系比这个目标更大。',terms:'infertility · fertility treatment · grief · couple relationship · limits',psychAnsEn:'Fertility journeys can create grief, comparison, and a loss of control. Use appropriate medical evaluation, protect intimacy from becoming only a task, and share the emotional burden with a partner or counselor.',psychSupplementEn:'Your body is not a moral scorecard. Let medical care guide the facts and let compassion protect the person living through the uncertainty.',psychSupplementZh:'身体不是道德成绩单。让医疗照看事实，让慈悲保护正在经历不确定的你。'},
'离婚带娃、单亲妈妈/爸爸怕养不好孩子':{nameEn:'Single parenting after divorce',queryEn:'I am raising my child alone after the divorce. I am afraid I will not do it well. I worry about what this does to my child.',searchEn:'single parent divorce child parenting guilt support',en:'Children need one steady adult more than a perfect family shape. Keep routines predictable, do not let the child carry adult conflict, and arrange practical help for yourself.',enZh:'孩子需要的是一个稳定的大人，而不是完美的家庭形态。让日常可预期，别让孩子背大人的冲突，也为自己安排实际的帮忙。',terms:'single parenting · routine · parental conflict · support network · co-parenting',psychAnsEn:'Children are harmed more by chronic conflict than by a calm single-parent home. Protect routines, avoid using the child as a messenger, build a support network, and care for your own stability.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not have to be two parents at once. One steady, loving, supported caregiver can be a strong home.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必一个人同时成为两个父母。一个稳定、有爱、被支持的照顾者，就能成为坚实的家。'},
'职场被领导PUA、当众贬低打压':{nameEn:'Workplace manipulation and humiliation',queryEn:'My manager puts me down in front of everyone. He keeps criticizing me and I feel worthless at work. I dread going in every day.',searchEn:'workplace bullying PUA abusive manager humiliation gaslighting boundaries',en:'Repeated humiliation is a workplace problem, not proof about you. Record what happened with dates, refuse to discuss it in public, and treat HR, a union or leaving as real options.',enZh:'反复被羞辱是职场问题，不是关于你的证明。记下时间与事实，拒绝在有人的场合谈，把人力、工会或离职当成真实选项。',terms:'workplace abuse · documentation · boundary · escalation · leaving options',psychAnsEn:'Healthy management addresses work; manipulation attacks your worth and creates dependence. Document events, reality-check with trusted people, protect boundaries, and plan an exit or formal complaint when needed.',psychSupplementEn:'Someone’s contempt is not a reliable measurement of your ability. Keep your evidence, your allies, and a path toward safety.',psychSupplementZh:'别人的轻蔑不是衡量能力的可靠尺子。保留证据、伙伴和通向安全的道路。'},
'孩子厌学、不肯上学、休学在家':{nameEn:'School refusal and a child who will not attend',queryEn:'My child refuses to go to school. He stays home all day and will not leave the house. I do not know what to do.',searchEn:'school refusal child anxiety bullying education home study',en:'School refusal is usually a symptom, not defiance. Look for bullying, anxiety or learning problems first, keep contact with the school, and treat it as a mental health matter with a professional.',enZh:'厌学往往是症状，不是对抗。先排查被欺负、焦虑或学习困难，和学校保持联系，并把它当心理健康问题交给专业人士处理。',terms:'school refusal · anxiety · bullying · school liaison · assessment',psychAnsEn:'School refusal is usually a signal of anxiety, learning difficulty, bullying, or family stress rather than laziness. Listen first, solve the barrier, coordinate with school and professionals, and return in small steps.',psychSupplementEn:'A child hiding from school may be hiding from pain, not responsibility. Become a safe base before asking for brave steps.',psychSupplementZh:'躲开学校的孩子，可能是在躲痛苦，而不是逃避责任。先成为安全的基地，再邀请他勇敢迈步。'},
'身材容貌焦虑、总觉得自己不好看':{nameEn:'Body image and appearance anxiety',queryEn:'I hate how I look. I worry about my body and my face all the time. I cannot look at photos of myself.',searchEn:'body image appearance anxiety ugly weight mirror photos self esteem',en:'Appearance worry grows with mirror time and comparison. Reduce checking and editing, value the body for what it does, and seek help if appearance thoughts keep you from going out.',enZh:'容貌焦虑随照镜子和比较一起长大。减少反复检查与修图，把身体的价值放回"它能做什么"，如果因为这些念头不敢出门，请寻求帮助。',terms:'body image · appearance checking · comparison · body functionality · support',psychAnsEn:'Appearance anxiety is amplified by edited images and selective attention. Reduce comparison triggers, shift toward what the body can do, and seek assessment when appearance concerns disrupt eating, work, or social life.',psychSupplementEn:'Your body is not a display item waiting for a score. It is the place where your life is happening and deserves care.',psychSupplementZh:'身体不是等待打分的展品。它是生命正在发生的地方，值得被照顾。'},
'在学校被孤立排挤、被同学冷落针对':{nameEn:'School isolation and relational bullying',queryEn:'I am left out at school and no one talks to me. My classmates exclude me on purpose. I feel alone every day.',searchEn:'school bullying isolation exclusion rumors classmates social anxiety',en:'Being excluded hurts, and it is not evidence that you are unlovable. Tell one adult who can actually act, build one friendship outside that group, and keep your own interests alive.',enZh:'被排挤很疼，但它不能证明你不值得被喜欢。找一个真正能处理的大人说，在这个圈子外建立一段友谊，别把自己的兴趣丢掉。',terms:'school exclusion · belonging · trusted adult · alternative friendship · interests',psychAnsEn:'Relational bullying is real harm, not evidence that you are defective. Record incidents, find one safe connection, involve trusted adults and school procedures, and prioritize safety over forced conformity.',psychSupplementEn:'Not belonging to one group does not mean belonging nowhere. Seek one safe person and let support begin there.',psychSupplementZh:'不属于一个群体，不等于无处归属。先找到一个安全的人，让支持从那里开始。'},
'孩子在学校被欺负、被打、被孤立，家长怎么办':{nameEn:'When a child is bullied at school',queryEn:'My child is being bullied and hit at school. I do not know whether to talk to the teacher or to the other parents. I want to protect my child.',searchEn:'child bullied school parent hit violence bullying evidence teacher safety',en:'Take it seriously and act in writing. Ask the child for facts without blame, report it to the school formally, require a safety plan, and involve the police when there is violence.',enZh:'认真对待，并且留下书面记录。先不带责备地问清事实，正式向学校报备，要求给出安全方案；涉及暴力时报警。',terms:'school bullying · documentation · safety plan · school meeting · police report',psychAnsEn:'First reassure the child that it is not their fault, then document injuries and incidents, contact the school through clear procedures, and seek legal or emergency help when safety is threatened. Do not demand that the child fight back.',psychSupplementEn:'Your child needs to know that asking for protection is brave. Stand beside them without making revenge the plan.',psychSupplementZh:'孩子需要知道，求助和要求保护本身就是勇敢。站在他身边，但不要把报复当成计划。'},
'总遇渣男渣女、恋爱脑上头、一谈就卑微':{nameEn:'Repeated harmful relationships and losing yourself in love',queryEn:'I keep ending up with people who treat me badly. I lose myself when I fall in love. I know it is wrong but I cannot leave.',searchEn:'toxic relationships dating red flags love addiction low self worth',en:'A repeated pattern needs a rule, not another explanation. Name the early warning signs you have seen before, keep your own life and friends, and leave at the first clear violation.',enZh:'反复出现的模式，需要一条规则，而不是再解释一次。写下你以前见过的早期信号，保住自己的生活和朋友，第一次明确越界就走。',terms:'relationship pattern · red flags · boundary · self-worth · dating rule',psychAnsEn:'Repeatedly choosing harmful partners can reflect familiar attachment patterns and early idealization. Slow the pace, watch consistency and how a person treats others, set financial and emotional boundaries, and seek support for the pattern.',psychSupplementEn:'You are not “a magnet for bad people.” You are a person learning to recognize safety, and learning can change the pattern.',psychSupplementZh:'你不是“吸引坏人的体质”。你只是正在学习辨认安全，而学习可以改变模式。'},
'谈婚论嫁因为钱崩了：彩礼、房子、嫁妆谈不拢':{nameEn:'Marriage conflict over money and property',queryEn:'We broke up over money before getting married. We cannot agree on the bride price, the house or the dowry. Our families are fighting about it.',searchEn:'marriage money conflict bride price dowry house finances family negotiation',en:'Money arguments are usually about security and fairness. Put the real numbers and expectations on paper, separate what is negotiable from what is not, and bring in a neutral third party.',enZh:'钱上的争执，多半关乎安全感和公平。把真实数字和期待写下来，分清可谈与不可谈，必要时请一位中立的第三方。',terms:'money conflict · expectations · negotiation · fairness · third party',psychAnsEn:'Money arguments often carry questions about respect, security, boundaries, and family influence. Discuss the couple’s shared plan, separate relatives’ expectations, document major agreements, and notice whether conflict can be repaired.',psychSupplementEn:'A wedding is a form; the daily partnership is the substance. Choose a conversation where both people can be honest without turning love into a price tag.',psychSupplementZh:'婚礼是形式，日常的共同生活才是实质。选择一次诚实的谈话，不要把爱变成价格标签。'},
'被家暴了、被打第一次、要不要原谅、怎么自保':{nameEn:'Domestic violence and personal safety',queryEn:'My partner hit me for the first time. I do not know whether to forgive him. I am afraid and I do not know how to keep myself safe.',searchEn:'domestic violence abuse hit safety plan shelter police protection',en:'Violence is never something you caused, and safety comes before forgiveness. Move to a safe place with documents and money, tell someone you trust, and contact a hotline or the police.',enZh:'暴力从来不是你造成的，安全排在原谅之前。先带着证件和钱转移到安全的地方，告诉可信任的人，并联系求助热线或报警。',terms:'domestic violence · safety plan · hotline · police · documentation',psychAnsEn:'Violence is not your fault and an apology does not make a safety plan unnecessary. Prioritize immediate safety, preserve evidence, contact emergency services or domestic-violence support, and plan with trusted people rather than confronting danger alone.',psychSupplementEn:'Compassion never asks you to remain where you are being harmed. Protecting your life is not selfish; it is the first responsible step.',psychSupplementZh:'慈悲不会要求你留在被伤害的地方。保护生命不是自私，而是最先要承担的责任。'},
'胎停/流产后走不出来、怕再怀又失去':{nameEn:'Pregnancy loss and fear of trying again',queryEn:'I lost the baby and I cannot move on. I am afraid it will happen again if I get pregnant.',searchEn:'miscarriage pregnancy loss grief self blame fear pregnancy again',en:'Early loss is a real bereavement and deserves to be spoken about. Let yourself grieve without a deadline, ask for medical follow-up, and bring your partner into it instead of carrying it alone.',enZh:'胎停流产是真实的丧失，值得被说出来。允许自己哀伤、不必设期限，做一次医学随访，把伴侣拉进来，别一个人扛。',terms:'pregnancy loss · grief · medical follow-up · couple support · mourning',psychAnsEn:'Pregnancy loss is a real bereavement and is usually not caused by an ordinary mistake or failure to be careful. Follow medical recovery advice, seek evaluation when losses recur, and allow grief without rushing into another pregnancy.',psychSupplementEn:'Your grief is legitimate, and self-blame is not a duty. Let your body and heart recover at a pace that respects what happened.',psychSupplementZh:'你的悲伤是真实的，自责不是义务。让身体和心以尊重这段经历的速度恢复。'},
'男人压力大、有苦说不出、扛不住了也不敢哭':{nameEn:'Men under pressure who feel unable to speak',queryEn:'I am under pressure all the time but I cannot talk about it. I am not supposed to cry or show weakness. I hold it in alone.',searchEn:'men stress cannot cry masculinity depression anger provider pressure',en:'The rule that a man must carry everything silently costs lives. Say one true sentence to one person, use the free counseling or hotline that exists, and treat crying as regulation, not failure.',enZh:'"男人必须自己扛"这条规矩是要付出生命代价的。先对一个人说一句真话，用上已有的免费咨询或热线，把哭看成调节，不是失败。',terms:'male role strain · help seeking · emotional expression · hotline · counseling',psychAnsEn:'Emotional suppression can show up as irritability, withdrawal, sleep problems, substance use, or physical symptoms. Speaking honestly, sharing practical load, moving the body, and seeking professional help are forms of strength, not weakness.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not have to be a wall for everyone. Let someone stand beside you before the weight becomes dangerous.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必成为所有人的墙。在重量变得危险前，让一个人站到你身边。'},
'退休后失落、突然没事干、觉得自己没用了':{nameEn:'Retirement loss and feeling useless',queryEn:'Since I retired I feel lost and useless. I have nothing to do and no one needs me. I do not know what I am for now.',searchEn:'retirement depression identity loss empty purpose older adults',en:'Retirement removes a role faster than it offers a new one. Build a weekly structure in advance, keep one contribution that uses your skill, and let the first months feel strange.',enZh:'退休拿走角色的速度，比给你新角色更快。提前搭好一周的结构，保留一件用得上你本事的事，并允许头几个月就是别扭的。',terms:'retirement · role loss · weekly structure · contribution · purpose',psychAnsEn:'Retirement can remove structure, identity, social contact, and a sense of being needed at once. Build a new rhythm through relationships, interests, contribution, and health while allowing a transition period.',psychSupplementEn:'A role ended; a life did not. Your worth is not limited to what an employer needed from you.',psychSupplementZh:'一个角色结束了，生命没有结束。你的价值不只来自雇主曾经需要你做什么。'},
'更年期情绪失控、莫名想哭、容易发火、潮热出汗':{nameEn:'Menopause mood changes and hot flashes',queryEn:'I am going through menopause and my mood is out of control. I cry for no reason and get hot flashes at night.',searchEn:'menopause mood swings hot flashes crying irritability sleep hormones',en:'Perimenopause changes mood and sleep through hormones, not through character. Get a proper clinical assessment, treat sleep and hot flushes, and keep exercise and steady social contact.',enZh:'更年期的情绪与睡眠受激素影响，不是人品问题。做一次规范的就诊评估，处理睡眠与潮热，同时保持运动和稳定的社交。',terms:'perimenopause · hormonal mood change · sleep · assessment · exercise',psychAnsEn:'Perimenopause can affect sleep, mood, and body temperature through hormonal changes. Seek medical evaluation for persistent or severe symptoms, protect sleep, reduce triggers, and distinguish treatable depression from ordinary mood shifts.',psychSupplementEn:'This body transition is not a character flaw. You deserve medical care, patience, and a home that responds with understanding rather than mockery.',psychSupplementZh:'身体的过渡不是性格缺陷。你值得医疗照顾、耐心，以及一个用理解而非嘲笑回应你的家。'},
'信息过载、刷新闻越刷越焦虑':{nameEn:'Information overload and news anxiety',queryEn:'I keep scrolling the news and feel more anxious. There is too much information every day. I am afraid of missing something.',searchEn:'information overload news anxiety social media doomscrolling screen sleep',en:'Anxiety grows with how often you check, not with how much you know. Set fixed times for news, choose two reliable sources, and stop scrolling at least an hour before sleep.',enZh:'焦虑跟"你查得多勤"有关，跟"你知道多少"无关。把看新闻定在固定时段，只留两个可靠来源，睡前至少一小时停止刷。',terms:'information overload · doomscrolling · news limits · reliable sources · sleep',psychAnsEn:'More information does not automatically create more safety. Set two short news windows, use reliable sources, and stop checking before sleep. Separate what you can act on from what you cannot control.',psychSupplementEn:'Caring about the world does not require exhausting yourself. Protect a quiet part of the day so compassion can last.',psychSupplementZh:'关心世界不等于耗尽自己。每天保护一段安静时间，慈悲才能持续。'},
'同事冲突、不会沟通、工作关系紧张':{nameEn:'Workplace conflict and difficult communication',queryEn:'I do not get along with my coworkers. We clash and I do not know how to talk to them. The office feels tense every day.',searchEn:'coworker conflict communication workplace tension boundaries',en:'Workplace friction is easier to handle with facts and boundaries. Describe the specific behavior rather than the person, ask for what you need in one clear sentence, and keep a record.',enZh:'职场摩擦，用事实和界限来处理更容易。说具体的行为、不说人，把需要缩成一句清楚的话，并留下记录。',terms:'workplace conflict · assertive communication · specific behavior · boundary · record',psychAnsEn:'Separate the person from the problem. Describe the observable behavior, its impact, and a clear request instead of guessing motives or attacking character.',psychSupplementEn:'Communication is not a contest to win. Say what reduces the chance of further harm, then release the need to control the other person.',psychSupplementZh:'沟通不是为了赢过对方。说清什么能减少继续受伤的可能，然后放下控制对方的需要。'},
'朋友渐行渐远、关系变淡':{nameEn:'Friends growing distant',queryEn:'My old friends and I have drifted apart. We barely talk now. I miss how close we used to be.',searchEn:'friends drifting apart friendship fading loneliness reconnect',en:'Friendships fade through neglect rather than through falling out. Send one specific message, propose a simple fixed meeting, and accept that some friendships belong to an earlier season.',enZh:'友情多半是淡掉的，不是吵没的。发一条具体的消息，约一次固定而简单的见面，并接受有些朋友属于过去的季节。',terms:'friendship maintenance · adult friendship · initiative · life season · acceptance',psychAnsEn:'Friendships change with distance, life stages, and available energy. Send one warm, low-pressure message, then allow the other person’s response to guide how much you invest.',psychSupplementEn:'A changing friendship does not erase what was real. Thank the connection, and make room for new forms of belonging.',psychSupplementZh:'变化中的友情不会抹掉曾经的真实。感谢这段连接，也为新的归属留出空间。'},
'宠物离世、失去陪伴走不出来':{nameEn:'Grief after losing a beloved pet',queryEn:'My cat died and I cannot stop grieving. People say it was just a pet, but it felt like losing family. I miss him every day.',searchEn:'pet loss grief cat dog death companion mourning',en:'Losing an animal companion is a real bereavement that others may not recognize. Say the loss out loud, keep a small ritual, and find people who understand this kind of grief.',enZh:'失去陪伴动物是真实的丧亲，别人可能不认。把这份失去说出来，留一个小小的仪式，找到懂这种痛的人。',terms:'pet loss · disenfranchised grief · ritual · memorial · support',psychAnsEn:'Pet loss is a real relationship loss. Give yourself permission to grieve, create a small farewell ritual, and do not rush to replace the bond or punish yourself for past decisions.',psychSupplementEn:'The love was real because the life was shared. Let the memory become tenderness rather than a demand to stop grieving.',psychSupplementZh:'这份爱是真实的，因为你们共同生活过。让记忆变成温柔，而不是要求自己立刻停止悲伤。'},
'长期照顾家人、照顾者耗竭':{nameEn:'Caregiver burnout and family caregiving',queryEn:'I have been taking care of my family member for a long time. I am exhausted and have no time for myself. I feel guilty when I rest.',searchEn:'caregiver burnout family caregiving exhaustion compassion fatigue respite',en:'Caregiver burnout builds when nobody is caring for the caregiver. Arrange scheduled relief, give other family members named tasks, and ask the doctor about respite services.',enZh:'照护者的耗竭，来自没有人来照顾照护者。安排固定的喘息时间，把任务分配到具体人头上，并向医生了解喘息服务。',terms:'caregiver burnout · respite care · task sharing · relief · limits',psychAnsEn:'Caregiver burnout is a depletion of resources, not a lack of love. Share tasks, arrange rotation or professional help, protect regular sleep and meals, and ask before reaching crisis.',psychSupplementEn:'Resting does not abandon the person you care for. It protects the relationship and the strength needed to continue.',psychSupplementZh:'休息不是抛下被照顾的人，而是在保护这段关系和继续照顾所需的力量。'},
'搬家后不适应、新城市孤独':{nameEn:'Moving to a new city and feeling lonely',queryEn:'I moved to a new city and feel lonely. I miss home and I have no friends here. I do not feel settled.',searchEn:'moving new city homesick loneliness relocation adjustment',en:'A new city takes about a year to feel familiar. Build routines in the first weeks, repeat one place until you are recognized there, and expect the loneliness instead of treating it as failure.',enZh:'一座新城大约要一年才熟起来。头几周先建立日常路线，重复去同一个地方，直到那里有人认得你；把孤独当作过程，而不是失败。',terms:'relocation · adaptation · routine · social contact · adjustment period',psychAnsEn:'Moving interrupts routines, relationships, and a sense of identity. Build three anchors: one familiar route, one place where you can greet people, and one steady connection. Familiarity grows through repetition.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not have to love the new place immediately. A home can be built slowly through ordinary acts of kindness.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必立刻喜欢新地方。家可以通过日常的小小善意慢慢建成。'},
'怕第一印象不好、见面就失常':{nameEn:'Fear of making a bad first impression',queryEn:'I am afraid of making a bad first impression. I get nervous and say the wrong things when I meet someone important.',searchEn:'first impression interview nerves dating performance primacy effect being judged',en:'First impressions matter, but not in the way you fear. People remember the opening most, so choose one impression to leave—reliable, warm, or professional—instead of trying to show everything at once. Turn your attention toward what you want to learn about the other person.',enZh:'第一印象确实重要，但起作用的方式和你担心的不一样。人记开头记得最牢，所以别想一次展现全部，只挑一个要留下的印象——可靠、亲切或专业。把注意力转到"我想了解对方什么"。',terms:'first impression · primacy effect · performance pressure · shift of attention · genuine opening',psychAnsEn:'The primacy effect means early information shapes how everything later is read. Reduce the pressure to show everything, prepare one honest opening line, and move attention outward from being judged to understanding the other person.',psychSupplementEn:'One meeting sets a starting point, not a verdict. Be sincere in this moment and let the relationship unfold in its own time.',psychSupplementZh:'一次见面定的是起手，不是判决。此刻真诚就好，剩下的关系会自己慢慢展开。'},
'容易被光环骗、看人看走眼':{nameEn:'Dazzled by a halo and misjudging people',queryEn:'I am easily impressed by titles and appearance. I keep misjudging people and trusting the wrong ones.',searchEn:'halo effect trust judgment dating charisma character seeing people clearly',en:'One bright quality makes the mind fill in the rest, so competence starts to look like character. Keep three separate ledgers: promises kept, behavior under stress, and how the person treats those below them.',enZh:'一个亮点会让大脑自动补全其余部分，于是"能干"看起来就像"人品好"。分开记三本账：答应的事做到几件、遇麻烦时的反应、他怎么对待不如他的人。',terms:'halo effect · character judgment · trust · charisma · evidence over time',psychAnsEn:'The halo effect blends ability and character into one impression. Separate observation from inference, and let trust accumulate from repeated, specific evidence rather than from one impressive trait.',psychSupplementEn:'Give your impression freely, but give your trust by the piece. Time is not distrust; it is kindness to yourself.',psychSupplementZh:'印象可以先给，信任要按件给。用时间去验证，不是不信任对方，而是对自己温柔。'},
'被人贴标签、被偏见定义':{nameEn:'Being labeled and defined by prejudice',queryEn:'People put labels on me and judge me before they know me. I am tired of being defined by others.',searchEn:'stereotype labeling prejudice discrimination gender age judged by others',en:'A stereotype is the other person taking a shortcut, not a statement of fact. You do not have to accept the label or rush to disprove it; build a record of concrete work instead, and notice when you label others too.',enZh:'贴标签是对方在走捷径，不是在陈述事实。你不必收下这个标签，也不必急着自证；用一件件具体的事留下记录，同时留意自己也在给别人贴标签。',terms:'stereotype · stereotype threat · labeling · self-justification · evidence',psychAnsEn:'Stereotypes are mental shortcuts that persist because they save effort, not because they are accurate. Spend less energy on self-justification, keep the evidence of your work visible, and watch for your own labels about others.',psychSupplementEn:'A label can only stick if you hand it your self-worth. Do the work that matters and let a single comment stay a single comment.',psychSupplementZh:'标签能贴住你，是因为你把它接到了自我价值上。做你自己的事，让一句评价就只是一句评价。'},
'总觉得是别人的错、怪完又后悔':{nameEn:'Blaming others first and regretting it later',queryEn:'I always feel it is other people’s fault. I blame them and then regret what I said. I cannot stop myself.',searchEn:'blame attribution anger regret communication misunderstanding accountability',en:'The mind sees other people’s behavior but knows its own circumstances—so others look careless while you look reasonable. Before blaming, say the sentence again from their possible situation, and own your share when explaining your own mistakes.',enZh:'人看得见别人的行为，却清楚自己的难处——所以别人显得不靠谱，自己显得有道理。责怪前，先把那句话换成"他可能的处境"说一遍；解释自己的错时，先认下该认的那一段。',terms:'fundamental attribution error · actor-observer bias · blame · perspective · accountability',psychAnsEn:'The fundamental attribution error is an information gap rather than a character flaw. Deliberately consider situational explanations for others, and acknowledge your own part first so accountability reads as honesty rather than excuse-making.',psychSupplementEn:'Understanding someone’s situation is not excusing the harm. It only keeps your judgment accurate and your heart less inflamed.',psychSupplementZh:'理解对方的处境，不等于替伤害开脱。它只是让你的判断更准、心里那口气不那么冲。'},
'看不惯某个人、一见就有火':{nameEn:'Strong dislike and irritation toward one person',queryEn:'There is one person I cannot stand. Just seeing him makes me angry and I do not even know why.',searchEn:'dislike irritation projection annoyance hostility resentment judging others',en:'Strong irritation is information worth checking. Write the complaint in one concrete sentence and ask whether it could describe you too. If it can, that is self-knowledge; if it cannot, it may be a boundary problem.',enZh:'强烈的反感是值得检验的信息。把不满写成一句具体的话，问自己"这句能不能也说我"。能，就是照见；不能，多半是边界的问题。',terms:'projection · shadow · irritation · boundary · self-observation',psychAnsEn:'Projection means an unacceptable part of oneself is seen in someone else. Test the observation against yourself first, then decide whether this is your own material or a real boundary that needs a clear conversation.',psychSupplementEn:'Whatever this person stirs up is worth staying curious about. Curiosity turns resentment into understanding.',psychSupplementZh:'对方勾起来的那个反应，值得你先好奇而不是先下判。好奇会把怨气变成理解。'},
'融不进圈子、新环境谁都不认识':{nameEn:'Struggling to fit into a new circle',queryEn:'I cannot fit into the new circle. I do not know anyone here and cannot join the conversation. I feel like an outsider.',searchEn:'new environment fitting in strangers loneliness circle social contact familiarity',en:'Belonging grows through repetition more than through charm. Appear in the same places at the same times, greet the same faces, and aim to learn one name per visit—familiarity quietly becomes closeness.',enZh:'归属感靠的是重复，不是魅力。固定时间出现在固定的地方，跟同一批人打招呼，每次只记住一个名字——熟悉会悄悄变成亲近。',terms:'mere exposure effect · familiarity · belonging · repetition · social contact',psychAnsEn:'The mere exposure effect shows that repeated, low-pressure contact increases liking and a sense of safety. Choose a few fixed routines and places rather than trying to make one strong impression.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not need to be impressive to be included. Show up again, and let people grow used to your presence.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必够厉害才配被接纳。再来一次，让别人慢慢习惯有你在。'},
'付出很多却没人记情、关系不对等':{nameEn:'Giving a great deal and feeling unappreciated',queryEn:'I give a lot in this relationship and no one appreciates it. It always feels one sided. I am tired of being taken for granted.',searchEn:'reciprocity unequal relationship giving resentment boundaries appreciation',en:'Reciprocity is real, but a gift too large to repay is often forgotten rather than honored. Ask yourself whether you are giving or trading; if you are trading, say what you need directly instead of paying in sacrifice.',enZh:'礼尚往来是真的，但一份大到还不起的好，往往不是被记住，而是被绕开。先问自己：我是在给，还是在换？若是换，就直说要什么，别用委屈自己来付账。',terms:'reciprocity · equity · giving · resentment · direct request',psychAnsEn:'Reciprocity works best in amounts the other person can return. Reduce the size of what you give, distinguish generosity from an unspoken bargain, and make requests plainly instead of accumulating silent debt.',psychSupplementEn:'Give as one who is also being cared for. When you are not running on empty, your kindness comes without hidden cost.',psychSupplementZh:'给的时候，也把自己算进被照顾的人里。心里不空的时候，给出去的好才不藏账。'},
'越使劲越拧、怎么说都不听':{nameEn:'The harder you push, the more they resist',queryEn:'The more I push, the more they resist. I have said it a hundred times and nothing changes. They will not listen to me.',searchEn:'communication resistance persuasion parenting partner conflict listening warmth',en:'Wind cannot make a coat come off; warmth can. Pressure triggers defense, so describe what you see instead of judging, discuss one issue at a time, and keep the request small enough to accept.',enZh:'风再大也吹不掉大衣，暖一点反而会自己解开。压力会招来防御：先说看到的事实、不下评判，一次只谈一件事，要求小到对方答得上来。',terms:'south wind effect · warmth · psychological reactance · one issue · small request',psychAnsEn:'Pressure and criticism produce defense, while warmth lowers it—the south wind principle. Describe behavior, limit each conversation to one topic, and make requests concrete and small.',psychSupplementEn:'You can care about the outcome without forcing it. Speak so the other person can stay open, and let the change take its time.',psychSupplementZh:'你可以在意结果，但不必硬推。把话说得让对方接得住，改变就有时间发生。'},
'在外面忍着、回家就炸':{nameEn:'Holding it in outside and exploding at home',queryEn:'I hold everything in at work and then explode at home. I take it out on my family and feel guilty afterwards.',searchEn:'displaced anger kick the cat effect family temper guilt stress venting',en:'Anger travels down the path of least resistance—from the boss to you, from you to the family, from the family to the child. Take ten minutes outside the door to discharge it, and name what happened before it lands on someone you love.',enZh:'怒火会顺着阻力最小的路往下传：老板传给你，你传给家人，家人传给孩子。进门前先给自己十分钟把火卸掉，进家先说清发生了什么，别让它落在你最亲的人身上。',terms:'displaced aggression · kick the cat effect · emotion contagion · transition ritual · repair',psychAnsEn:'Displaced aggression is anger redirected from its source to a safer target. Build a transition ritual before entering home, name the real source honestly, and address the original conflict where it actually belongs.',psychSupplementEn:'Your family did not cause the fire. Let them be shelter rather than the place where it spreads.',psychSupplementZh:'这把火不是家人点的。让他们是你的屋檐，不是火蔓延的地方。'},
'有自伤念头、想死、觉得撑不下去了':{nameEn:'Thoughts of self-harm or not wanting to live',queryEn:'Sometimes I feel living is pointless and thoughts of hurting myself come up. These thoughts scare me. What should I do?',searchEn:'suicidal thoughts suicide self harm hurting myself hurt myself keep thinking about hurting myself thoughts of self injury not wanting to live do not want to live anymore do not want to live want to die do not want to live any more hopeless crisis safety',en:'If these thoughts are strong right now, contact a crisis line or emergency services immediately and make sure someone stays with you tonight — this is not something to carry alone. Pain this heavy is not a character flaw, and it can be reduced with real help. Move anything you could hurt yourself with out of reach, take tonight one hour at a time, and tell one person out loud that you are not okay.',enZh:'如果这种念头此刻很强烈，请立刻联系危机热线或急救，并确保今晚有人陪着你——这件事不该一个人扛。痛到这个程度不是你人品的问题，它可以通过真实帮助被减轻。先把可能伤到自己的东西移开，把今晚切成一个小时一个小时地过，并且对一个人说出"我很不好"。',terms:'suicidal ideation · crisis support · safety plan · means restriction · staying connected',psychAnsEn:'Suicidal thoughts usually signal pain that has exceeded a person’s current capacity to bear it, not a permanent verdict on a life. The immediate priorities are safety, crisis support, removing access to means, and telling someone; then professional care — therapy and, when indicated, medication — to treat the pain itself.',psychSupplementEn:'A thought is not a decision. Tonight your only task is to get through this one night with a person nearby.',psychSupplementZh:'念头不等于决定。今晚你唯一的任务，是有人在身旁，过完这一夜。'},
'被性侵、被性骚扰、不敢说':{nameEn:'Sexual assault or harassment and not daring to speak',queryEn:'I was assaulted or harassed and I have never told anyone. I keep feeling it was my fault and I cannot sleep.',searchEn:'sexual assault harassment assaulted trauma shame blame myself it was not my fault my fault happened to me survivor safety support keep evidence',en:'It was not your fault — what you wore, what time you went out, and whether you resisted change nothing about that. If the harassment is still happening, keep evidence and contact the police or a support service. See a doctor for your body and for peace of mind. Tell one person you trust, even a single sentence. Sleeplessness, flashbacks, shaking, and fear of closeness are common trauma responses, not proof that something is wrong with you.',enZh:'这不是你的错——你穿了什么、几点出门、有没有反抗，都不改变这一点。如果骚扰还在继续，留好证据，联系警方或相关支持机构。为身体、也为安心，去医院检查一次。找一个信得过的人说出来，哪怕只一句。失眠、闪回、发抖、怕亲近，都是常见的创伤反应，不是你有问题。',terms:'sexual violence · trauma response · self-blame · reporting · trauma-informed care',psychAnsEn:'Survivors of sexual violence often carry shame that belongs to the offender. Support includes physical safety, evidence preservation and reporting, medical care, and trauma-informed therapy. The pace of telling, forgiving, and recovering belongs to the survivor, not to anyone else’s timetable.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not owe anyone an explanation, a forgiveness, or a quick recovery. First safety, first medical care, first one person who believes you.',psychSupplementZh:'你不欠任何人一个解释、一个原谅或一次快速的恢复。先安全，先看医生，先找一个愿意相信你的人。'},
'幻听、觉得被监视、情绪忽高忽低':{nameEn:'Hearing voices, feeling watched, and extreme mood swings',queryEn:'Sometimes I hear voices others do not hear, or feel that people are watching and talking about me. My mood swings from very high to very low.',searchEn:'hearing voices paranoia feeling watched mood swings psychosis psychiatrist',en:'These experiences deserve a medical evaluation, not more self-discipline. Please see a psychiatrist or psychiatric clinic as soon as you can, and bring someone you trust. Write down when it happens, how often, and how it affects your sleep and eating. If you also have thoughts of not wanting to live, say so directly. This is a health condition, not a personal failure, and earlier treatment usually works better.',enZh:'这些体验需要的是医学评估，不是更强的自我克制。请尽快去精神科或心理科看医生，并带上一个你信任的人。把出现的时间、频率，以及对睡眠和吃饭的影响写下来带去。如果同时有不想活的念头，请直接说出来。这是一种健康状况，不是人品问题，越早治疗通常效果越好。',terms:'psychosis · early intervention · psychiatric assessment · sleep · support person',psychAnsEn:'Hearing voices, persistent beliefs of being watched or talked about, and marked mood swings need professional psychiatric assessment. Early evaluation and consistent treatment generally improve outcomes; steady sleep, family support, and avoiding alcohol or drugs all support recovery.',psychSupplementEn:'You are not crazy, and you are not alone in this. Getting assessed early is the kindest thing you can do for yourself.',psychSupplementZh:'你没有疯，这件事也不是只有你一个人遇到。越早评估，越是善待自己。'},
'查出抑郁症、不敢跟人说':{nameEn:'Diagnosed with depression and afraid to tell anyone',queryEn:'I was diagnosed with depression. I am afraid to tell anyone and afraid I will never get better. What should I do?',searchEn:'depressed depression diagnosis diagnosed with depression ashamed tell anyone never get better will it ever get better will my depression ever get better treatment medication antidepressant therapy stigma',en:'Depression is a common and treatable illness, not a weakness or a failure of attitude. You do not owe anyone the information; telling one trusted person is enough to begin. Follow the treatment plan — psychotherapy and, when prescribed, medication — and keep your follow-up visits. If thoughts of not wanting to live appear, get crisis help the same day.',enZh:'抑郁症是常见且可治疗的疾病，不是软弱，也不是态度问题。你没有义务告诉所有人，先告诉一个信得过的人就够开始了。按治疗计划走——心理治疗，以及医生开了就按时吃药——并把复诊跟住。如果出现不想活的念头，当天就寻求危机帮助。',terms:'depression · diagnosis · stigma · treatment adherence · crisis safety',psychAnsEn:'A diagnosis names a treatable condition; it is not a verdict on your life. Care usually combines psychotherapy, medication when indicated, steady sleep, daylight, and movement. The most important steps now are keeping appointments and following the prescription rather than deciding alone to stop.',psychSupplementEn:'You are allowed to keep this private while you get help. Let one person stand close to you, and let the treatment work over weeks, not days.',psychSupplementZh:'你可以先保密，同时把治疗做起来。让一个人靠近你，让治疗按周而不是按天起效。'},
'抑郁到不想动、起不来床':{nameEn:'Depression so heavy you cannot get out of bed',queryEn:'When I am depressed I cannot get up, wash, or eat. I lie in bed all day and feel useless. What can I do?',searchEn:'depression cannot get out of bed no energy no motivation no motivation to do anything cannot do anything lying in bed all day feel useless worthless cannot wash myself cannot eat behavioral activation',en:'This is not laziness; depression suppresses the brain systems that generate drive and reward. Shrink the goal until it cannot fail — sit up for thirty seconds, drink water, stand on the balcony — and count that as done. If you stop eating or sleeping entirely for days, tell your doctor promptly.',enZh:'这不是懒，是抑郁压住了产生动力和奖赏的脑内系统。把目标切到小到不可能失败——坐起来三十秒、喝口水、到阳台站一会儿——做到就算完成。如果几天完全吃不下、睡不着，尽快告诉医生。',terms:'behavioral activation · anhedonia · avolition · tiny steps · clinical review',psychAnsEn:'Loss of drive is a core symptom of depression, not a character flaw. Behavioral activation starts with actions so small they cannot fail, then lets activity itself feed back into mood. Tell your clinician if eating and sleeping stop.',psychSupplementEn:'Do not audit the whole day. Ask only whether you can move one step in front of you. That step is the day.',psychSupplementZh:'不要审一整天的账，只问脚下这一步动得动。动了，今天就算数。'},
'吃抗抑郁药难受、怕依赖、想停药':{nameEn:'Antidepressant side effects and the wish to stop',queryEn:'My antidepressant makes me nauseous, sleepy, and heavier. I heard it is addictive. I want to stop now that I feel a bit better. Can I?',searchEn:'antidepressant side effects stop taking antidepressant withdrawal dependence addicted to antidepressants how long to take ssri weight gain nausea',en:'Most antidepressants need two to four weeks to work, and early side effects often ease after the first week or two. They are not addictive the way alcohol or nicotine are; the difficulty is a withdrawal reaction. Never stop abruptly on your own — doing so is one of the most common causes of relapse. Log the side effects and bring them to your prescriber.',enZh:'多数抗抑郁药要两到四周才起效，初期的副作用常在头一两周后减轻。它们不像烟酒那样成瘾，麻烦的是撤药反应。不要自己骤停——突然停药是复发最常见的原因之一。把副作用记下来，带去给开药的医生看。',terms:'SSRI · onset time · side effects · discontinuation syndrome · relapse risk',psychAnsEn:'Antidepressants are not addictive substances; they act more like a scaffold. Early side effects are common and often settle. Tapering must be managed by the prescriber, because abrupt withdrawal brings symptoms and sharply raises relapse risk.',psychSupplementEn:'Wanting to be free of medicine is understandable. Bring that wish to the doctor rather than acting on it alone.',psychSupplementZh:'想不吃药的心情可以理解。把这个想法带去给医生说，别自己动手。'},
'抑郁好了又犯、看不到头':{nameEn:'Depression that keeps coming back',queryEn:'My depression keeps coming back. I get better and then crash again. Will it ever end? Living like this is exhausting.',searchEn:'depression relapse recurring depression coming back again will I ever get better hopeless exhausting maintenance treatment relapse signature',en:'Recurring depression is common and does not mean it is untreatable. Finishing the full course of treatment, rather than stopping when you feel better, is the best-documented way to reduce relapse. Build a relapse plan: list your earliest warning signs and who to call when they appear. If thoughts of not wanting to live return, treat it as an emergency.',enZh:'抑郁反复很常见，不等于治不好。把疗程走完、而不是感觉好了就停，是目前最能降低复发的办法。做一份复发预案：写下最早的预警信号，以及出现时打给谁。如果又出现不想活的念头，按紧急情况处理。',terms:'relapse · maintenance treatment · relapse signature · early warning signs · safety plan',psychAnsEn:'Depression is often episodic and relapsing. Longer maintenance treatment, attention to sleep and stress, and a written early-warning plan reduce how often and how hard episodes return. Recurrence is a course to manage, not proof that you failed.',psychSupplementEn:'You are not back at the start. You are on a road you have walked before, and this time you know its turns.',psychSupplementZh:'你不是回到起点，你是走在一条走过的路上，这次你认得它的弯。'},
'家人朋友抑郁了、不知道怎么陪':{nameEn:'How to support a family member or friend with depression',queryEn:'Someone I love is depressed. I want to help but I do not know what to say and I am afraid of saying the wrong thing.',searchEn:'supporting someone with depression what to say to a depressed friend help my depressed partner my husband is depressed my wife is depressed my partner is depressed family member depression how to help afraid of saying the wrong thing caregiver',en:'Presence matters more than words. Go with them to the doctor, treat them as ill rather than lazy or dramatic, do concrete small things, and listen without correcting. If they mention death or not wanting to live, ask directly — asking does not plant the idea — remove access to means, stay with them, and contact a doctor or crisis line. Caregivers need support too.',enZh:'在场比说得好更重要。陪他去看医生，把他当病人而不是懒人或矫情，做些具体的小事，听他说话而不急着纠正。如果他提到死、提到不想活，直接问出来——问不会把念头种进去——收好危险物品、陪着他，并联系医生或危机热线。陪的人也需要支持。',terms:'caregiver support · being present · listening · direct suicide question · means restriction',psychAnsEn:'Effective support means practical help, not advice: going with someone to treatment, reducing daily burden, listening without judgement, and taking any mention of self-harm or death seriously by asking directly and removing means.',psychSupplementEn:'You do not have to fix the illness. Stay nearby, do the practical thing in front of you, and let the professionals carry what is theirs to carry.',psychSupplementZh:'你不必把病治好。待在旁边，做眼前那件具体的事，专业的部分交给专业的人。'},
'微笑抑郁、看起来挺好、心里是空的':{nameEn:'Smiling depression: looking fine on the outside, empty inside',queryEn:'Everyone thinks I am cheerful and normal, but when I am alone I feel hollow and panicky. Have I been faking it all along?',searchEn:'smiling depression high functioning depression look fine on the outside appear normal cheerful nobody believes I am depressed hiding how i feel fake smile pretend to be ok empty inside',en:'"Smiling depression" is not a formal diagnosis; it describes a pattern in which the core symptoms are all present — low mood, loss of interest, poor sleep, a sense of emptiness — while outward functioning still holds, sometimes looking cheerful. That does not mean you are faking. The danger is precisely that "you seem fine" becomes the reason help gets postponed. Judge yourself by your symptoms, not by your appearance: take a PHQ-9 and get a professional assessment. Find one place, or one person, with whom you do not have to smile. If thoughts of not wanting to live appear, call a crisis line (12356) the same day.',enZh:'「微笑抑郁」不是正式诊断名，它描述的是一种状态：核心症状都在——情绪低、没兴趣、睡不好、心里空——但外头的功能还撑着，甚至看着开朗。这不等于你在装。危险恰恰在于"你看着挺好"成了拖延求助的理由。用症状判断自己，别用外表判断：做一次 PHQ-9，再去让专业人士评估。找一个不用你笑的地方，或一个不用你笑的人。如果冒出不想活的念头，当天就打危机热线（12356）。',terms:'smiling depression · high-functioning depression · concealment · delayed help-seeking · suicide risk',psychAnsEn:'High-functioning presentations of depression keep outward functioning largely intact while core symptoms persist, which delays recognition and help-seeking. Assessment and treatment follow the same lines as any depression: professional evaluation, psychotherapy, medication when indicated, and a written safety plan.',psychSupplementEn:'Looking fine was never evidence that you are fine. Let one person see the part you keep covered.',psychSupplementZh:'看着没事，从来不能证明你没事。让一个人看看你一直盖着的那部分。'},
'病耻感、要不要告诉单位、该不该请假':{nameEn:'Stigma, telling your workplace, and whether to take sick leave',queryEn:'I am afraid to let my workplace know I am ill. I fear being labeled and hurting my career, but hiding it is wearing me down. What should I do?',searchEn:'stigma mental illness at work telling my boss employer human resources disclose sick leave medical leave fear of being judged losing my job discrimination career impact cannot keep going',en:'What you fear is not only shame but your livelihood, and that is a real concern. Stigma is a documented barrier to seeking care. Disclosure can be layered rather than all-or-nothing: tell the few who need to know — your direct manager about workload, HR about leave procedures — in functional terms, without naming the diagnosis. In many jurisdictions illness brings sick leave and protected medical periods, and a sick note need not state the diagnosis (check local rules and your contract). Long-term concealment is itself exhausting and worsens depression, so set a horizon such as "two weeks first, then reassess". If thoughts of not wanting to live appear, work comes second — call a crisis line (12356).',enZh:'你怕的不只是丢脸，是丢饭碗，这份担心是实在的。病耻感是被文献证实的求助障碍。说不必是全说或全瞒，可以分层：只告诉必须知道的人——直属领导谈工作量，人事谈请假流程——用功能层面的说法，不必报诊断名。在多数地区，患病享有病假和医疗期保护，病假条上也不一定写诊断（请以当地法规和合同为准）。长期瞒着本身极耗人，也会加重抑郁，所以给自己定个期限，比如"先请两周，之后再看"。如果冒出不想活的念头，工作往后放，先打 12356。',terms:'stigma · disclosure · accommodation · sick leave · medical period · anti-discrimination',psychAnsEn:'Stigma delays help and worsens outcomes. Evidence-based practice is selective disclosure — telling only those who need the information, in functional terms — together with knowing your leave and accommodation rights. Concealment carries a real psychological cost, so it helps to give it a time limit rather than leaving it open-ended.',psychSupplementEn:'You may keep your diagnosis private and still ask for what you need. Protecting your livelihood and protecting your health are not opposites.',psychSupplementZh:'你可以不公开诊断，同时争取到需要的安排。保住饭碗和保住身体，不是二选一。'},
'情绪低落多久算抑郁、要不要去看医生':{nameEn:'How long low mood must last to count as depression, and when to see a doctor',queryEn:'I have been feeling low for quite a while now. Does that count as depression? At what point should I go and see a doctor?',searchEn:'how long does sadness last depression two weeks low mood for weeks should i see a doctor see a psychiatrist when to get help how long is too long depression test',en:'Duration, symptom count, and impaired functioning matter more than how bad it feels. A common threshold is low mood or loss of interest most of the day, nearly every day, for two weeks or more; shorter spells after a loss or a shock are usually a stress reaction, not a disorder. Mood that stays low but milder for two years or more may be persistent depression. The most practical test is function — work, study, self-care, relationships. One exception: thoughts of not wanting to live need same-day help (12356), whatever the duration. Start with a PHQ-9; being assessed is not the same as being diagnosed.',enZh:'判断关键不是"多难受"，而是持续时间、症状条数与功能受损。常用门槛是：几乎每天、大半天情绪低落或丧失兴趣，持续两周以上；遇到打击后短期的低落多是应激反应，还够不上障碍。程度不重却持续两年以上的，可能是持续性抑郁。最实用的判据是功能——上班、上学、照顾自己、关系有没有被拖垮。一个例外：出现不想活的念头，当天就要求助（12356），不用等两周。可以先做一次 PHQ-9；去评估不等于确诊。',terms:'duration criteria · two-week threshold · functional impairment · persistent depression · help-seeking threshold',psychAnsEn:'Depression is assessed by duration, symptom count, and functional impairment rather than by how bad the distress feels. Two weeks of persistent low mood or loss of interest is the usual threshold; a PHQ-9 supports screening, while a clinician makes the diagnosis. Seek help immediately, not in two weeks, if there are thoughts of not wanting to live.',psychSupplementEn:'Asking whether it is "really" depression is already a good reason to have it checked. Assessment costs little; waiting is what costs.',psychSupplementZh:'会问"我这算不算抑郁"，本身就是一个去看一看的理由。评估不费什么，拖下去才费。'},
'孩子说不想活、抑郁了、家长怎么办':{nameEn:'My child does not want to live: teen depression and what parents should do',queryEn:'My child told me they do not want to live, or has been diagnosed with depression and stays shut in their room. How do I talk to them and help?',searchEn:'my teenager wants to die suicidal teenager child depression teen depression my child self harms stays in room school refusal how to help suicidal thoughts parenting',en:'Treat the words as true: most children who say this are not making threats but asking for help, and this is one of the highest-risk moments. Ask directly — whether they have thought about how, whether anything is prepared, and when. Asking does not plant the idea; vagueness is what is dangerous. Remove access to means (medication, blades, ropes, reachable windows) and avoid leaving them alone for long. Get a psychiatric appointment or call a crisis line (12356); with a plan or any action taken, go to the emergency department. Note that teen depression often looks like irritability, outbursts, and school refusal rather than sadness, so it is easily mistaken for a phase. Say less, stay more.',enZh:'把孩子说的话当真：多数孩子说出这句话不是威胁，而是求救，这也是风险最高的时刻之一。要直接问——有没有想过怎么死、有没有准备东西、什么时候。直接问不会把念头种进去，含糊绕开才危险。收好危险物品（药物、刀片、绳索、可攀爬的窗户），这段时间别让他长时间独处。尽快挂精神科，或打危机热线（12356）；如果有明确计划或已行动，直接去急诊。要注意青少年抑郁常表现为易激惹、发脾气、厌学，而不是悲伤，所以很容易被当成叛逆期。少说教，多在场。',terms:'adolescent depression · irritability · direct suicide inquiry · means restriction · emergency referral',psychAnsEn:'Adolescent depression often presents as irritability and behavioural change rather than classic sadness. Evidence supports asking directly about suicidal thoughts, restricting access to means, reducing acute stressors, and prompt professional or emergency involvement. Parents need support too.',psychSupplementEn:'Your first job is not to reason your child out of it. It is to make sure they are safe tonight, and to let them know they are not being abandoned.',psychSupplementZh:'你第一件要做的不是把孩子劝通，是保证他今晚是安全的，并让他知道你没有放弃他。'},
'查不出病、浑身难受、是不是想出来的':{nameEn:'Tests are normal but my body hurts everywhere: is it all in my head?',queryEn:'I have been to several hospitals and all the tests come back normal, yet I feel unwell all over. Am I just being dramatic?',searchEn:'tests are normal but i feel sick all over physical symptoms of depression somatization medically unexplained symptoms body aches normal test results health anxiety keep checking am i imagining it',en:'"No abnormality found" does not mean "nothing is wrong". Depression and anxiety very often speak through the body — headaches, dizziness, palpitations, chest tightness, stomach and bowel trouble, widespread pain, numbness, fatigue. This is called somatization. Once the appropriate tests have been done and several hospitals agree, repeated testing tends to reinforce the fear of serious illness and makes the cycle worse. Your distress is real; its source lies where body and mind meet, not in an organ that has broken. When you see a doctor, say the emotional part out loud, and consider a psychiatric or psychosomatic clinic. If thoughts of not wanting to live appear, call a crisis line (12356).',enZh:'"查不出异常"不等于"没有问题"。抑郁和焦虑非常常借身体说话——头疼、头晕、心慌、胸闷、胃肠不适、浑身疼、发麻、疲乏，这叫躯体化。该做的检查做完、几家医院结论一致之后，反复检查反而会强化"我有重病"的恐惧，让循环更糟。你的难受是真的，它的来处在身心交界，而不是某个坏掉的器官。看病时把情绪那一面说出来，可以考虑精神科或心身医学科。如果出现不想活的念头，打 12356。',terms:'somatization · medically unexplained symptoms · normal test results · health anxiety · integrated care',psychAnsEn:'Somatization is common in depression and anxiety. Best practice is to complete the indicated investigations, then stop repeating them, address the emotional dimension explicitly, and treat the underlying condition; physical symptoms usually improve alongside mood.',psychSupplementEn:'You are not imagining it, and you are not being dramatic. The body was simply the first place the distress could be spoken.',psychSupplementZh:'你不是想出来的，也不是矫情。只是那份难受，最先从身体说了出来。'}
};
